COLLDATA("tadabburen","en",[[185,"§Al-Anfal\ndeeds\nInvoke Allah persistently that He reconciles the hearts of your Muslim brothers.\nSay, frequently, “There is no might and no power except by Allah”, and “Allah suffices me, there is none worthy of worship but Him. I have placed my trust in Him, He is the Lord of the Majestic Throne.”\nLook up the reason for the revelation of this verse, share it with friends, and draw lessons from it, or circulate it in a message.\nguid\nIf brotherhood is truly based on faith, it removes resentment and hatred from within the hearts.\nAllah’s care through knowledge, support and victory is for the patient believers, not those who lose hearts and the doubters.\nNo matter how powerful a servant thinks he is, he still needs Allah’s mercy because he, in fact, is weak and helpless.\nrefl\nوَأَلَّفَ بَيۡنَ قُلُوبِهِمۡۚ لَوۡ أَنفَقۡتَ مَا فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ جَمِيعٗا مَّآ أَلَّفۡتَ بَيۡنَ قُلُوبِهِمۡ وَلَٰكِنَّ ٱللَّهَ أَلَّفَ بَيۡنَهُمۡۚ\nIbn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \"When Allah brings the hearts together, nothing can draw them apart,\" then he read this verse. Ibn Kathir: 2/309.\nIf you want to bring your brethren's hearts together, what is the most important thing to start with?\nوَأَلَّفَ بَيۡنَ قُلُوبِهِمۡۚ لَوۡ أَنفَقۡتَ مَا فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ جَمِيعٗا مَّآ أَلَّفۡتَ بَيۡنَ قُلُوبِهِمۡ وَلَٰكِنَّ ٱللَّهَ أَلَّفَ بَيۡنَهُمۡۚ إِنَّهُۥ عَزِيزٌ حَكِيمٞ ٦٣\nMeaning: Allah brought together the hearts of the Aws and Khazraj. Reconciling the hearts of feuding Arab tribes was a miracle of the Prophet (ﷺ), as before that when one of them is slapped on his face, he never rests until he avenges it. They were the most proud among all people, but Allah brought them together through faith to the extent that a man would fight against his father and brother for the religion of Islam. Al-Qurtubi: 10/67.\nTrue faith has its signs upon the community. Explain.\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلنَّبِيُّ حَسۡبُكَ ٱللَّهُ وَمَنِ ٱتَّبَعَكَ مِنَ ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ ٦٤\nThis is a promise from Allah to His believing servants who follow His Messenger (ﷺ) that He will suffice and support them against their enemies. Therefore, if they take proper measures, namely believing and following the Prophet (ﷺ), He will surely suffice them with regard to what concerns them of both spiritual and worldly matters. That support will not be granted when its conditions are not met. Al-Saadi: 325\nWhat are the conditions of Allah's support and help for His allies?\nإِن يَكُن مِّنكُمۡ عِشۡرُونَ صَٰبِرُونَ يَغۡلِبُواْ مِاْئَتَيۡنِۚ وَإِن يَكُن مِّنكُم مِّاْئَةٞ يَغۡلِبُوٓاْ أَلۡفٗا مِّنَ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ بِأَنَّهُمۡ قَوۡمٞ لَّا يَفۡقَهُونَ ٦٥\n(For they are a people who do not understand), which means that they fight with no faith or clear insight, so they do not endure. Ibn Juzay: 1/348.\nThis verse mentions an irrefutable condition for victory, what is it?\nإِن يَكُن مِّنكُمۡ عِشۡرُونَ صَٰبِرُونَ يَغۡلِبُواْ مِاْئَتَيۡنِۚ وَإِن يَكُن مِّنكُم مِّاْئَةٞ يَغۡلِبُوٓاْ أَلۡفٗا مِّنَ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ بِأَنَّهُمۡ قَوۡمٞ لَّا يَفۡقَهُونَ ٦٥\n(They are a people who do not understand), they have no knowledge of what Allah has prepared for those who strive in His cause, so they fight in order to become supreme in the land and to spread mischief therein, whereas you understand the purpose of fighting, which is to make the word of Allah supreme, cause His religion to prevail, defend the Book of Allah, and to attain the greatest success with Allah. All of these are basis for courage, steadfastness and determination to fight. Al-Saadi: 326.\nWhat is the importance of understanding the meanings behind Jihad to overcome the enemies?\nتُرِيدُونَ عَرَضَ ٱلدُّنۡيَا وَٱللَّهُ يُرِيدُ ٱلۡأٓخِرَةَۗ وَٱللَّهُ عَزِيزٌ حَكِيمٞ ٦٧\n(You desire), O believers, (the perishable goods of this world), by accepting ransom, (but Allah desires the Hereafter) He wants for you the reward of the Hereafter by defeating the polytheists, and supporting the religion of Allah, and Allah is All-Mighty, All-Wise. Al-Baghawi: 2/239.\nDuring battle, many different intentions surface, so what is the intention favored by Allah?\nتُرِيدُونَ عَرَضَ ٱلدُّنۡيَا وَٱللَّهُ يُرِيدُ ٱلۡأٓخِرَةَۗ وَٱللَّهُ عَزِيزٌ حَكِيمٞ ٦٧\n(The perishable goods of this world), it is wealth, and it is called perishable goods because people's enjoyment of it is very brief; similar to a quick passage of a moving object. Ibn Ashur: 10/76.\nWhat is (the perishable goods of this world)? Why is it called as such?\nwords\nحَسبَكَSufficient for you\nحَرِّضِUrge\nيُثخِنَKills in excess"],[186,"§Al-Anfal\ndeeds\nDonate some of your money to a charitable organization, so you may be among those who fight with their wealth.\nBe kind to an expatriate in your country, and give him refuge, if necessary, as Allah praised the Ansar for giving shelter to their brethren, Almuhajireen.\nDo something to maintain the ties with your kinship, such as teaching, feeding, or fulfilling their needs, as they are more entitled than others.\nguid\nAllah, the Almighty, cannot be defeated nor be outrun.\nIt is the duty of every Muslim to help his Muslims brethren when they seek his help in religion.\nBeware of alliance with the disbelievers, for it is a persecution and a great corruption.\nrefl\nوَٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ وَلَمۡ يُهَاجِرُواْ مَا لَكُم مِّن وَلَٰيَتِهِم مِّن شَيۡءٍ حَتَّىٰ يُهَاجِرُواْۚ وَإِنِ ٱسۡتَنصَرُوكُمۡ فِي ٱلدِّينِ فَعَلَيۡكُمُ ٱلنَّصۡرُ إِلَّا عَلَىٰ قَوۡمِۢ بَيۡنَكُمۡ وَبَيۡنَهُم مِّيثَٰقٞۗ\nIbn Al-Arabi said: \"When oppressed Muslims are held captives, the allegiance with them still holds, and helping to free them is a duty on us at all costs. Fulfilling this duty either by force, if the number of our forces suffices, or by paying ransom money, no matter how much it costs, until the last Dirham, as stated by Imam Malik and all scholars. We belong to Allah, and to Him we shall return for what happened to Muslims as they left their brethren held captives, when they have excess of wealth, capability, number of forces, power and stamina.\" Al-Qurtubi: 10/347.\nDescribe our Islamic duty toward oppressed Muslim captives.\nوَإِنِ ٱسۡتَنصَرُوكُمۡ فِي ٱلدِّينِ فَعَلَيۡكُمُ ٱلنَّصۡرُ إِلَّا عَلَىٰ قَوۡمِۢ بَيۡنَكُمۡ وَبَيۡنَهُم مِّيثَٰقٞۗ وَٱللَّهُ بِمَا تَعۡمَلُونَ بَصِيرٞ ٧٢\n(And Allah is All-Seeing of what you do), this is a warning to Muslims, not to fight against others with whom they have a binding treaty, out of compassion for other Muslims. This indicates the importance of the fulfillment of a covenant, and the fact that it cannot be breached except for a clear reason under its conditions. Ibn Ashur: 10/87.\nThe verse concludes with (and Allah is All-Seeing of what you do). What does that indicate?\nوَٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ بَعۡضُهُمۡ أَوۡلِيَآءُ بَعۡضٍۚ إِلَّا تَفۡعَلُوهُ تَكُن فِتۡنَةٞ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ وَفَسَادٞ كَبِيرٞ ٧٣\nAllah ended the allegiance between the disbelievers and believers, and made the believers allies of one another, and the disbelievers allies of one another. Al-Qurtubi: 10/87\nWhat is the risk of the absence of the allegiance and renunciation in Muslims’ lives?\nوَٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ بَعۡضُهُمۡ أَوۡلِيَآءُ بَعۡضٍۚ إِلَّا تَفۡعَلُوهُ تَكُن فِتۡنَةٞ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ وَفَسَادٞ كَبِيرٞ ٧٣\nMeaning: The disbelievers possess a strong drive to have allegiance to one another against you, and a great inclination to pursue that, despite the existence of intense enmity between them since you are a party and they are all one party gathered in disbelief by the call of satan, while you are gathered in faith by the call of the Most Merciful. Al-Biqai: 3/252.\nDespite their differences, the disbelievers agree and have allegiance to one another on one thing. What is it?\nوَٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ بَعۡضُهُمۡ أَوۡلِيَآءُ بَعۡضٍۚ إِلَّا تَفۡعَلُوهُ تَكُن فِتۡنَةٞ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ وَفَسَادٞ كَبِيرٞ ٧٣\n(Unless you do likewise), taking believers as allies and opposing the disbelievers...(there will be persecution in the land and a great corruption), and that will lead to unlimited evil, because of confusing truth with falsehood, believers with disbelievers, and because of the cessation of major acts of worship such as Jihad, Hijrah (migration), and other aims of Sharia, which will be missed if the believers do not take only the believers as allies and protectors. Al-Saadi: 328.\nGive some examples of corruption that may occur if disbelievers are not opposed.\nوَٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ وَهَاجَرُواْ وَجَٰهَدُواْ فِي سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِ وَٱلَّذِينَ ءَاوَواْ وَّنَصَرُوٓاْ أُوْلَٰٓئِكَ هُمُ ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنُونَ حَقّٗاۚ\n(They are the true believers because they confirmed their faith by means of the deeds that they undertook, namely migration, mutual support, forming an alliance with one another, and striving in Jihad against their enemies, the disbelievers and hypocrites. Al-Saadi: 328.\nWhat are the traits of true believers?\nوَٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ مِنۢ بَعۡدُ وَهَاجَرُواْ وَجَٰهَدُواْ مَعَكُمۡ فَأُوْلَٰٓئِكَ مِنكُمۡۚ وَأُوْلُواْ ٱلۡأَرۡحَامِ بَعۡضُهُمۡ أَوۡلَىٰ بِبَعۡضٖ فِي كِتَٰبِ ٱللَّهِۚ\nThis brotherhood of faith, which appeared at the beginning of Islam, had a great impact and was of a great significance, because the Prophet (ﷺ) established a special bond of brotherhood between the Muhajireen and Ansar, something that surpassed the regular bonds of brotherhood, as they even used to inherit one another by virtue of this brotherhood. Then, Allah revealed the words: (But blood relatives are more entitled to inherit from one another according to the Book of Allah). Therefore, no one can inherit from a person except his relatives. Al-Saadi: 328.\nGive an example showing the importance of alliance between the believers during the early period of Islam.\nwords\nفَأَمكَنَ مِنهُمHe empowered you over them\nآوَواThey gave shelter [to the Emigrants]\nوَأُولُوBlood relatives"],[187,"§At-Tawbah\ndeeds\nLook for the names of Surah At-Tawbah, and the reasons behind these names, then draw three useful lessons from that.\nMaintain your prayer and give to charity, so that your sins may be forgiven.\nRead the words of Allah to non-Muslims around you in the hope that they become guided.\nguid\nAllah and His Messenger (ﷺ) had disassociated themselves from the polytheists, so, what is your position on them?\nReflect on how Allah calls on the enemies of Islam to repent and revert to Him, while promising to reward them if they do, then think about what Allah would offer the believers.\nOne of the most effective ways of calling others to Allah is to let them listen to the verses of the Holy Quran or its trprotection, then grant him protection so that he may hear the words of Allah [the Qurananslation].\nrefl\nبَرَآءَةٞ مِّنَ ٱللَّهِ وَرَسُولِهِۦٓ إِلَى ٱلَّذِينَ عَٰهَدتُّم مِّنَ ٱلۡمُشۡرِكِينَ ١\nAli bin Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Al-Basmalah, (In the Name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful), is a protection and this Surah (Bara’ah) was revealed with the sword, and that is why it does not begin with the protection. Ibn Juzay: 1/350.\nThe absence of Al-Basmalah at the beginning of this Surah indicates the forceful dealing of the Quran with the stubborn disbelievers. Explain.\nبَرَآءَةٞ مِّنَ ٱللَّهِ وَرَسُولِهِۦٓ إِلَى ٱلَّذِينَ عَٰهَدتُّم مِّنَ ٱلۡمُشۡرِكِينَ ١\nAllah says, ([This is] a declaration of disassociation by Allah and His Messenger to those polytheists with whom you have made a treaty), these treaties were discretionary, not binding ones. Hence Muslims had the choice between affirming or negating them. Ibn Taimyah: 3/300.\nWere the treaties with the polytheists discretionary or binding ones?\nوَأَذَٰنٞ مِّنَ ٱللَّهِ وَرَسُولِهِۦٓ إِلَى ٱلنَّاسِ يَوۡمَ ٱلۡحَجِّ ٱلۡأَكۡبَرِ أَنَّ ٱللَّهَ بَرِيٓءٞ مِّنَ ٱلۡمُشۡرِكِينَ وَرَسُولُهُۥۚ\nThis is a command to the Muslims to inform the polytheists of this disassociation, lest the Muslims be considered deceitful. Ibn Ashur: 10/108\nWhy were the Muslims commanded to inform the polytheists of this disassociation?\nفَإِن تَابُواْ وَأَقَامُواْ ٱلصَّلَوٰةَ وَءَاتَوُاْ ٱلزَّكَوٰةَ فَخَلُّواْ سَبِيلَهُمۡۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ غَفُورٞ رَّحِيمٞ ٥\nThis verse is used as a proof that when one says, \"I repent,\" then his statement is not considered sufficient until he combines it with deeds to achieve repentance, as Allah requires here establishing prayer and giving zakah in order to reach true repentance. Al-Qurtubi: 10/114.\nWhat do you say to one who repents with words only?\nفَإِن تَابُواْ وَأَقَامُواْ ٱلصَّلَوٰةَ وَءَاتَوُاْ ٱلزَّكَوٰةَ فَخَلُّواْ سَبِيلَهُمۡۚ\nHere, Allah mentions the most important aspects of Islam, including what is less important. Surely, the highest pillar of Islam after the profession of faith (the Shahada) is prayer, which is the right of Allah, the Exalted and Ever High, then zakah, which benefits the poor and needy, and is considered the most honorable act associated with people. This is why Allah often mentions the prayer and zakah together. Ibn Kathir: 2/321.\nAmong all acts of worship, prayer and zakah are singled out for mention. Why?\nوَإِنۡ أَحَدٞ مِّنَ ٱلۡمُشۡرِكِينَ ٱسۡتَجَارَكَ فَأَجِرۡهُ حَتَّىٰ يَسۡمَعَ كَلَٰمَ ٱللَّهِ ثُمَّ أَبۡلِغۡهُ مَأۡمَنَهُۥۚ ذَٰلِكَ بِأَنَّهُمۡ قَوۡمٞ لَّا يَعۡلَمُونَ ٦\nMeaning: If he asks for your protection, which is your safeguarding and care, then, grant him that so he can listen to the Quran, and understand its rulings, commands and prohibitions. If he accepts that, then it is for the better; otherwise deliver him to his place of safety. Al-Qurtubi: 10/114.\nExplain the reason for giving safety to a disbeliever.\nوَإِنۡ أَحَدٞ مِّنَ ٱلۡمُشۡرِكِينَ ٱسۡتَجَارَكَ فَأَجِرۡهُ حَتَّىٰ يَسۡمَعَ كَلَٰمَ ٱللَّهِ\n(So that he may hear the words of Allah), the Quran. Recite the Quran to him, and mention a good part of the religion with which you establish Allah's proof against him. This, and similar endeavors, caused many of them to find guidance. Ibn Kathir: 2/322.\nWhat is wisdom behind having the polytheists listen to the Quran?\nwords\nوَأَذَانٌAn announcement\nلَم يَنقُصُوكُمThey have not broken the covenant with you\nانسَلَخَPassed\nوَاحصُرُوهُمBesiege them\nاستَجَارَكَHe seeks your protection"],[188,"§At-Tawbah\ndeeds\nLook for a deed that you like, but Allah hates, and leave it in fear of Him.\nMaintain your daily prayer on time and in congregation.\nSay, \"O Allah, I ask You to grant me fear of You in private and in public. I ask You to make me true in speech in times of contentment and of anger.\"\nguid\nDo not feel secure with non-Muslims, and do not surrender yourself and your neck to them, no matter what their promises are, as they cannot be trusted.\nThe brotherhood in Islam is proven by three things: Oneness of Allah, establishing prayer and giving zakah.\nReviling the religion is apostasy and disbelief, which justifies death and fighting others over it.\nrefl\nٱشۡتَرَوۡاْ بِـَٔايَٰتِ ٱللَّهِ ثَمَنٗا قَلِيلٗا فَصَدُّواْ عَن سَبِيلِهِۦٓۚ إِنَّهُمۡ سَآءَ مَا كَانُواْ يَعۡمَلُونَ ٩\nThey exchanged that for (a small price), worthless vanities of the world, which are their desires and whims that they followed. This verse explains the preceding one, (and most of them are defiantly disobedient), whoever follows his whims and lustful desires, will become defiantly disobedient. Al-Alusi: 5/251.\nIn light of this verse, describe the risk of following whims on the Muslim's faith.\nلَا يَرۡقُبُونَ فِي مُؤۡمِنٍ إِلّٗا وَلَا ذِمَّةٗۚ\nThe reason why they are described as hostile toward you and as hating you is the issue of faith, so defend your faith and support it; take those who oppose it as your enemies and take those who support it as your allies and friends, basing your relationships with others on that criteria; do not base the issue of friendship or enmity on personal inclinations, whims and desires, and do not follow the soul that prompts one to evil with regard to this matter. Al-Saadi: 330.\nWhat is the wisdom behind focusing on the \"belief\" in (toward a believer)? What lesson should be learned from this for a Muslim?\nفَإِن تَابُواْ وَأَقَامُواْ ٱلصَّلَوٰةَ وَءَاتَوُاْ ٱلزَّكَوٰةَ فَإِخۡوَٰنُكُمۡ فِي ٱلدِّينِۗ ( ونفصل الآيات لقوم يعملون )\nBrotherhood in Islam is conditional upon repentance from shirk, establishing prayer, and giving zakah. If these conditions are not met, then a person cannot be considered a brother in Islam. Ibn Taimyah: 3/311\nCan a person, who does not pray, be considered a brother in Islam?\nفَإِن تَابُواْ وَأَقَامُواْ ٱلصَّلَوٰةَ وَءَاتَوُاْ ٱلزَّكَوٰةَ فَإِخۡوَٰنُكُمۡ فِي ٱلدِّينِۗ\n(If they repent), repent from shirk, (establish prayer and give zakah, then they are your brothers), indeed, they become your brothers (in religion), they have the same rights as yours, and carry out the same duties as you do. Al-Baghawi: 2/253.\nWhat are the foundations by which brotherhood is realized among the believers?\nوَطَعَنُواْ فِي دِينِكُمۡ\nReviling is ascribing inappropriate things to the religion, or objecting, in an irreverential manner, to a religious ruling that is definite and supported by a clear evidence. Al-Qurtubi: 10/123.\nWhat is reviling the religion?\nفَقَٰتِلُوٓاْ أَئِمَّةَ ٱلۡكُفۡرِ\nThey are singled out for mention because of the seriousness of their offence, and because others follow them. This also highlights the fact that whoever reviles Islam and takes it upon himself to oppose it, is one of the leaders of disbelief. Al-Saadi: 330.\nThe leaders of disbelief are singled out for mention. Why?\nأَتَخۡشَوۡنَهُمۡۚ فَٱللَّهُ أَحَقُّ أَن تَخۡشَوۡهُ إِن كُنتُم مُّؤۡمِنِينَ ١٣\nThe condition clause, (if you are truly believers) is used in this verse -even though it is certain- in order to stimulate their religious devotion, so they would prove that they are true believers who fear Allah, not the people. Ibn Ashur: 10/134.\nThe condition clause: (if you are truly believers) is used in this verse. Why?\nwords\nاستَقَامُواFulfilled their covenant\nوَإِن يَظهَرُواIf they were to overcome you\nنَكَثُواThey breached\nأَيمَانَهُمTheir treaties and covenants\nلاَ أَيمَانَThere are no oaths sacred to them"],[189,"§At-Tawbah\ndeeds\nWrite an article or a letter exposing the hypocrites' methods for corrupting the society or their enmity toward Islam.\nStay in the mosque to remember and worship Allah before or after any prayer, or between sunset and nightfall, for that is maintenance of the mosque.\nAsk Allah to bless you with fear of Him, as it is the greatest sign of guidance.\nguid\nis inevitable that you encounter afflictions and tests from Allah to show whether you are sincere in your faith or not.\nBeware of seeking alliance with enemies of Islam.\nGood deeds are void in the absence of sincere belief in the Oneness of Allah.\nrefl\nقَٰتِلُوهُمۡ يُعَذِّبۡهُمُ ٱللَّهُ بِأَيۡدِيكُمۡ وَيُخۡزِهِمۡ وَيَنصُرۡكُمۡ عَلَيۡهِمۡ وَيَشۡفِ صُدُورَ قَوۡمٖ مُّؤۡمِنِينَ ١٤\nAllah encourages the believers and explains the wisdom behind ordaining Jihad against them, and all the while He is able to destroy their enemies with a command from Him: (Fight them, Allah will punish them at your hands, disgrace them, give you victory over them, and will soothe the hearts of a believing people). Ibn Kathir: 2/325.\nAllah ordains Jihad against enemies, even though He can destroy them with one command. Why?\nوَيَشۡفِ صُدُورَ قَوۡمٖ مُّؤۡمِنِينَ ١٤ وَيُذۡهِبۡ غَيۡظَ قُلُوبِهِمۡۗ\nThis is indicative of Allah's love and care for the believers, as He made one of the aims of Sharia is this heartfelt satisfaction and causing their rage to recede. Al-Saadi: 331.\nThis verse is indicative of Allah's love and care for the believers. Explain.\nوَيَتُوبُ ٱللَّهُ عَلَىٰ مَن يَشَآءُۗ وَٱللَّهُ عَلِيمٌ حَكِيمٌ ١٥\nThis verse concludes with (Allah is All-Knowing, All-Wise) to indicate that Allah treats people based on what He knows of their intentions. He is all-Wise Who does not ordain but what manifests wisdom, hence, it is the duty of people to follow His ordinances. Ibn Ashur: 10/137.\nThis verse concludes with: (Allah is All-Knowing, All-Wise), why?\nإِنَّمَا يَعۡمُرُ مَسَٰجِدَ ٱللَّهِ مَنۡ ءَامَنَ بِٱللَّهِ وَٱلۡيَوۡمِ ٱلۡأٓخِرِ وَأَقَامَ ٱلصَّلَوٰةَ وَءَاتَى ٱلزَّكَوٰةَ وَلَمۡ يَخۡشَ إِلَّا ٱللَّهَۖ فَعَسَىٰٓ أُوْلَٰٓئِكَ أَن يَكُونُواْ مِنَ ٱلۡمُهۡتَدِينَ ١٨\nAllah makes clear that the maintainers of mosques are those who fear none but Allah. Whoever fears Allah only, puts his hope and trust solely in Him, as hope and fear are correlated. Those who visit shrines (grave sites) to invoke the dead, humble themselves to them, worship them, and have fear and hope from other than Allah are just like the polytheists who place their fear and hope in their idols. Ibn Taimyah: 3/327.\nWhat are the difference between the maintainers of mosques and those of shrines?\nإِنَّمَا يَعۡمُرُ مَسَٰجِدَ ٱللَّهِ مَنۡ ءَامَنَ بِٱللَّهِ وَٱلۡيَوۡمِ ٱلۡأٓخِرِ وَأَقَامَ ٱلصَّلَوٰةَ وَءَاتَى ٱلزَّكَوٰةَ وَلَمۡ يَخۡشَ إِلَّا ٱللَّهَۖ فَعَسَىٰٓ أُوْلَٰٓئِكَ أَن يَكُونُواْ مِنَ ٱلۡمُهۡتَدِينَ ١٨\nAs for the one who does not believe in Allah nor the Last Day, and does not he fear Allah, he is not one of the maintainers of the mosques of Allah, nor is he one of their people to whom they belong, even if he claims to be as such. Al-Saadi: 331.\nWhat is the sign of the accepted maintenance of the mosques by Allah?\nأَجَعَلۡتُمۡ سِقَايَةَ ٱلۡحَآجِّ وَعِمَارَةَ ٱلۡمَسۡجِدِ ٱلۡحَرَامِ كَمَنۡ ءَامَنَ بِٱللَّهِ وَٱلۡيَوۡمِ ٱلۡأٓخِرِ وَجَٰهَدَ فِي سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِۚ لَا يَسۡتَوُۥنَ عِندَ ٱللَّهِۗ وَٱللَّهُ لَا يَهۡدِي ٱلۡقَوۡمَ ٱلظَّٰلِمِينَ ١٩\nMeaning: They claimed that they were the people and maintainers of the Sacred Mosque, but Allah calls them (the wrongdoing people) for their shirk; thus, maintaining and serving Allah's House will not benefit them at all. Ibn Kathir: 2/327.\nFor one who does not believe in the Oneness of Allah, does his good deed benefit him?\nأَجَعَلۡتُمۡ سِقَايَةَ ٱلۡحَآجِّ وَعِمَارَةَ ٱلۡمَسۡجِدِ ٱلۡحَرَامِ كَمَنۡ ءَامَنَ بِٱللَّهِ وَٱلۡيَوۡمِ ٱلۡأٓخِرِ وَجَٰهَدَ فِي سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِۚ لَا يَسۡتَوُۥنَ عِندَ ٱللَّهِۗ وَٱللَّهُ لَا يَهۡدِي ٱلۡقَوۡمَ ٱلظَّٰلِمِينَ ١٩\nThe reason of revelation of this verse is that some people from the tribe of Quraish bragged about providing water for the pilgrims and maintaining the Sacred Mosque in Makkah. Hence, Allah makes clear that Jihad in His cause is, in fact, much better than that. Ibn Juzay: 1/353.\nHow can you infer from this verse the disparity between deeds?\nwords\nوَلِيجَةًTrusted allies"],[190,"§At-Tawbah\ndeeds\nLook for a friend whom when you sit with, your faith increases, and keep him as a friend.\nIdentify something that distracts you from the love of Allah, then try to reduce your love for it.\nSay, \"O Allah, make what you have given me of the apparent and hidden blessings a reason for your pleasure and closeness to You, and let them not distract me from loving You.\"\nguid\nThe allegiance that is based on faith is greater and more noble than that which is based on kinship.\nVictory is solely from Allah; it is not by number, equipment or strength.\nThe faith of the soldiers and the sincerity of their trust in Allah is more important than their number and equipment.\nrefl\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ لَا تَتَّخِذُوٓاْ ءَابَآءَكُمۡ وَإِخۡوَٰنَكُمۡ أَوۡلِيَآءَ إِنِ ٱسۡتَحَبُّواْ ٱلۡكُفۡرَ عَلَى ٱلۡإِيمَٰنِۚ\n(Do not take your fathers and brothers as allies), who are the closest of people to you, so it is even more appropriate that you should not take as allies other people (if they choose disbelief over belief). Al-Saadi: 332.\nAllah singles out the fathers and brothers for mention, why?\nقُلۡ إِن كَانَ ءَابَآؤُكُمۡ وَأَبۡنَآؤُكُمۡ وَإِخۡوَٰنُكُمۡ وَأَزۡوَٰجُكُمۡ وَعَشِيرَتُكُمۡ وَأَمۡوَٰلٌ ٱقۡتَرَفۡتُمُوهَا وَتِجَٰرَةٞ تَخۡشَوۡنَ كَسَادَهَا وَمَسَٰكِنُ تَرۡضَوۡنَهَآ أَحَبَّ إِلَيۡكُم مِّنَ ٱللَّهِ وَرَسُولِهِۦ وَجِهَادٖ فِي سَبِيلِهِۦ فَتَرَبَّصُواْ حَتَّىٰ يَأۡتِيَ ٱللَّهُ بِأَمۡرِهِۦۗ وَٱللَّهُ لَا يَهۡدِي ٱلۡقَوۡمَ ٱلۡفَٰسِقِينَ ٢٤\nThis is a threat to whoever prefers his family, wealth or house over migration and Jihad in the cause of Allah. Ibn Juzay: 1/354.\nWhat is the risk of being over-attached to one's family, wealth or house?\nقُلۡ إِن كَانَ ءَابَآؤُكُمۡ وَأَبۡنَآؤُكُمۡ وَإِخۡوَٰنُكُمۡ وَأَزۡوَٰجُكُمۡ وَعَشِيرَتُكُمۡ وَأَمۡوَٰلٌ ٱقۡتَرَفۡتُمُوهَا وَتِجَٰرَةٞ تَخۡشَوۡنَ كَسَادَهَا وَمَسَٰكِنُ تَرۡضَوۡنَهَآ أَحَبَّ إِلَيۡكُم مِّنَ ٱللَّهِ وَرَسُولِهِۦ وَجِهَادٖ فِي سَبِيلِهِۦ فَتَرَبَّصُواْ حَتَّىٰ يَأۡتِيَ ٱللَّهُ بِأَمۡرِهِۦۗ وَٱللَّهُ لَا يَهۡدِي ٱلۡقَوۡمَ ٱلۡفَٰسِقِينَ ٢٤\nThis verse provides the greatest evidence for the obligation to love Allah and His Messenger (ﷺ), and to give them precedence over love of anything else. The sign of that is, if a person is presented with two options, one of which is loved by Allah and His Messenger (ﷺ), but he has no inclination toward it, and the other option is something that he loves and desires, but it will cause him to miss out on or will detract from the thing that is loved by Allah and His Messenger (ﷺ); if he gives precedence to what he himself desires over what Allah loves, then it is an indication that he is a wrongdoer who is not doing what he must. Al-Saadi: 332.\nHow can a servant prove his of love of Allah and His Messenger (ﷺ)?\nأَحَبَّ إِلَيۡكُم مِّنَ ٱللَّهِ وَرَسُولِهِۦ وَجِهَادٖ فِي سَبِيلِهِۦ فَتَرَبَّصُواْ حَتَّىٰ يَأۡتِيَ ٱللَّهُ بِأَمۡرِهِۦۗ وَٱللَّهُ لَا يَهۡدِي ٱلۡقَوۡمَ ٱلۡفَٰسِقِينَ ٢٤\nAmong all deeds that Allah loves of His servants, He singles out Jihad for mention because of its high status, and the risks associated with it, such as loss of life, spending of wealth, and leaving families behind, which make people more likely to lag behind when called for it; especially that when this Surah was revealed after the battle of Tabuk in which the hypocrites and some Muslims did not participate. Ibn Ashur: 10/153.\nIn this verse, Allah singles out Jihad for mention, why?\nلَقَدۡ نَصَرَكُمُ ٱللَّهُ فِي مَوَاطِنَ كَثِيرَةٖ\nAllah, the Exalted, reminds the believers how He favored and blessed them by granting them victory in many battles with His Messenger (ﷺ). Allah mentions that victory comes from Him, by His aid and decree, not because of their numbers or adequate supplies. Ibn Kathir: 2/328.\nWhat is the benefit of ascribing victory to Allah, the Almighty?\nوَيَوۡمَ حُنَيۡنٍ إِذۡ أَعۡجَبَتۡكُمۡ كَثۡرَتُكُمۡ فَلَمۡ تُغۡنِ عَنكُمۡ شَيۡـٔٗا وَضَاقَتۡ عَلَيۡكُمُ ٱلۡأَرۡضُ بِمَا رَحُبَتۡ ثُمَّ وَلَّيۡتُم مُّدۡبِرِينَ ٢٥\nIn the battle of Hunayn, the Muslim army consisted of twelve thousand soldiers, and some of them said: \"We will not be defeated today because of our number.\" So, Allah wanted to show their incapacity, and they started running away from Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) who stood firmly on his ride with few of his Companions, and prayed to Allah to send help. He then picked up a handful of earth, hurled it at the faces of the disbelievers while saying, \"May your faces be shameful.\" He called his people to return to the battlefield, which they did, and Allah defeated the disbelievers. Ibn Juzay: 1/354.\nThere is a lesson, In this verse, for the nation and for the fighters. Explain.\nوَيَوۡمَ حُنَيۡنٍ إِذۡ أَعۡجَبَتۡكُمۡ كَثۡرَتُكُمۡ فَلَمۡ تُغۡنِ عَنكُمۡ شَيۡٔا وَضَاقَتۡ عَلَيۡكُمُ ٱلۡأَرۡضُ بِمَا رَحُبَتۡ ثُمَّ وَلَّيۡتُم مُّدۡبِرِينَ ٢٥\nSome of the Muslim fighters said: \"We will not be defeated today because of our number.” So, Allah forsaken them to their words, and they were defeated at the beginning of the battle until they came back at their enemy. Al-Baghawi: 10/149.\nDescribe the risk of self-admiration on individuals and groups?\nwords\nاقتَرَفتُمُوهَاYou have acquired\nكَسَادَهَاA decline in it\nفَلَم تُغنِIt did not avail you at all"],[191,"§At-Tawbah\ndeeds\nWorship Allah by invoking Him with these two great names, and saying: \"O All-Forgiving, forgive me\" and \"O Most Merciful, have mercy on me.\"\nLearn Sharia rulings with regard to dealing with disbelievers and others, who live in a Muslim community.\nShare a message in which you explain that relying upon Allah is to abandon unlawful earning in fear of Him and trusting in His promise.\nguid\nThe fear of indigence and poverty does not prevent the believer from complying with the command of his Lord, for Allah gives glad tiding of enriching those who comply with His command.\nSeeking knowledge is not a justification for staying poor, or being a burden on others. There have existed many righteous scholars who were among the richest people.\nDo not obey the scholars in disobeying Allah, and do not be so fanatical about a scholar or an educator to the extent that you reject the truth for his sake. Be sincere in following Allah's Sharia only, and be keen to know the evidence.\nrefl\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوٓاْ إِنَّمَا ٱلۡمُشۡرِكُونَ نَجَسٞ\nThey are evil in their beliefs and actions, for what impurity could be worse than that of one who worships besides Allah other gods who can neither bring benefit nor cause harm, and cannot avail him anything? Their deeds vary between opposing Allah, averting people from the path of Allah, supporting falsehood, rejecting the truth, and spreading corruption in the land while making no effort to set things straight. Al-Saadi: 333.\nWhat is meant by the \"impurity\" of the polytheists?\nوَإِنۡ خِفۡتُمۡ عَيۡلَةٗ فَسَوۡفَ يُغۡنِيكُمُ ٱللَّهُ مِن فَضۡلِهِۦٓ إِن شَآءَۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ عَلِيمٌ حَكِيمٞ ٢٨\n(And If you fear poverty), which is destitution. The polytheists were used to bring foods to Makkah, so people feared shortage of sustenance if polytheists were prevented from coming to it. Allah promised them that He would enrich them out of His bounty, and so all Arab tribes accepted Islam, and food in Makkah became abundant, then Allah made them conquered the rest of towns. Ibn Juzay: 1/355.\nWhat is your advice to one who justifies consuming unlawful money with fear of poverty?\nوَإِنۡ خِفۡتُمۡ عَيۡلَةٗ فَسَوۡفَ يُغۡنِيكُمُ ٱللَّهُ مِن فَضۡلِهِۦٓ إِن شَآءَۚ\nThis is conditional upon His will, because being enriched in this world is not necessarily one of the outcomes of faith, and it does not indicate that Allah loves a person. Hence, Allah linked this matter to His will, for He may give worldly gain to one whom He loves and one whom He does not, but He does not grant faith and religious commitment except to one whom He loves. Al-Saadi: 333.\nAllah makes enriching conditional upon His will, why?\nقَٰتِلُواْ ٱلَّذِينَ لَا يُؤۡمِنُونَ بِٱللَّهِ وَلَا بِٱلۡيَوۡمِ ٱلۡأٓخِرِ وَلَا يُحَرِّمُونَ مَا حَرَّمَ ٱللَّهُ وَرَسُولُهُۥ وَلَا يَدِينُونَ دِينَ ٱلۡحَقِّ مِنَ ٱلَّذِينَ أُوتُواْ ٱلۡكِتَٰبَ حَتَّىٰ يُعۡطُواْ ٱلۡجِزۡيَةَ عَن يَدٖ وَهُمۡ صَٰغِرُونَ ٢٩\n(They hand in), with humility and defeat. Ibn Abbas (t) said: \"They give Jizyah (protection tax) with their own hands, and not send it through others.\" It is, also, said that they give it while acknowledging the favor of Muslims in accepting Jizyah from them. Al-Baghawi: 2/268.\nDescribe the honor of Muslims and humility of disbelievers in giving the Jizyah.\nوَلَا يَدِينُونَ دِينَ ٱلۡحَقِّ مِنَ ٱلَّذِينَ أُوتُواْ ٱلۡكِتَٰبَ\nThey do not follow the true religion, and even if they do claim to follow a religion, then it is not the correct religion because either it is a false religion that Allah did not prescribe in the first place, or it is an abrogated religion that Allah did prescribe, but He superseded it with the religion of Muhammad (ﷺ), therefore adhering to it after it has been abrogated is not permissible. Al-Saadi: 334.\nThe religion that is followed by people of Scripture is false in two ways. What are they?.\nٱتَّخَذُوٓاْ أَحۡبَارَهُمۡ وَرُهۡبَٰنَهُمۡ أَرۡبَابٗا مِّن دُونِ ٱللَّهِ\nAdi bin Hatim (t) reported: \"I came to the Prophet (ﷺ) while I had a cross of gold around my neck. He said: 'O Adi, remove this idol from yourself', and I did, then I came to him and heard him reciting (They have taken their rabbis and monks as lords besides Allah). I said: 'we do not worship them!'. He said: 'Is it not when they prohibit what Allah has made lawful for you, you consider it unlawful, and when they permit what Allah has made unlawful for you, you consider it lawful?' I said: 'yes.' He said: 'That is worshiping them'.\" Abdulla bin Al-Mubarak said: \"Had anyone changed the religion but the kings, the corrupted rabbis and monks?\" Al-Baghawi: 2/273.\nHow did rabbis and monks become as lords for their people besides Allah?\nٱتَّخَذُوٓاْ أَحۡبَارَهُمۡ وَرُهۡبَٰنَهُمۡ أَرۡبَابٗا مِّن دُونِ ٱللَّهِ\nThey accepted the sayings of their rabbis and monks, which are contrary to the fundamentals of their religion, and believed that the rabbis and monks forbid what is made lawful by Allah, and permitted what is made unlawful by Him. This was practiced uniformly by the followers of the two religions (Judaism and Christianity). This, in turn, led to the belief that some of these rabbis and monks had reached the rank of Lordship. Hence, this evil was stuck to both nations, despite the few among them who did not share the same belief, as Adi bin Hatim claimed, but a nation is held responsible for not forbidding the evil done by individuals. Ibn Ashur: 10/170.\nWhen does shirk become associated with forbidding and permitting?\nwords\nعَيلَةًPoverty\nيُضَاهِئُونَThey imitate\nأَنَّى يُؤفَكُونَHow can they be deluded from the truth"],[192,"§At-Tawbah\ndeeds\nReview the zakah of your wealth, and give a voluntary donation to charity.\nOne of the main reasons for the spread of polytheism and heresies is the money paid to the misleading clergymen.\nStarting today, operate using the Hijri months as much as you can, as they are the ones favored by Allah, and are among the manifestations of Islamic practice.\nguid\nThis is a statement that brings to light the hostility of Jewish and Christian leader to Islam, and their cooperation to corrupt it and its followers.\nGood news to Muslims that Islam will become the religion by which Allah is worshiped on Earth, and no other religions.\nThe wealth of those who do not pay the obligatory zakah will become hell for them on the Day of Resurrection.\nrefl\nيُرِيدُونَ أَن يُطۡفِـُٔواْ نُورَ ٱللَّهِ بِأَفۡوَٰهِهِمۡ وَيَأۡبَى ٱللَّهُ إِلَّآ أَن يُتِمَّ نُورَهُۥ وَلَوۡ كَرِهَ ٱلۡكَٰفِرُونَ ٣٢\nAttributing the light to the Holy Name of Allah indicates that their efforts to extinguish it are in vain, and they will never achieve their aim. Ibn Ashur: 10/172.\nWhat is the benefit of attributing the light to Allah?\nهُوَ ٱلَّذِيٓ أَرۡسَلَ رَسُولَهُۥ بِٱلۡهُدَىٰ وَدِينِ ٱلۡحَقِّ لِيُظۡهِرَهُۥ عَلَى ٱلدِّينِ كُلِّهِۦ وَلَوۡ كَرِهَ ٱلۡمُشۡرِكُونَ ٣٣\nMaking it prevail over all religions to be the highest and more powerful of all religions, spreading in all regions of the east and west. Ibn Juzay: 1/356.\nIn light of this verse, what do you say to one who despairs of the prevailing of Muslims?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوٓاْ إِنَّ كَثِيرٗا مِّنَ ٱلۡأَحۡبَارِ وَٱلرُّهۡبَانِ لَيَأۡكُلُونَ أَمۡوَٰلَ ٱلنَّاسِ بِٱلۡبَٰطِلِ وَيَصُدُّونَ عَن سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِۗ\nThis verse warns against corrupt scholars and misguided worshipers. Sufyan bin Uyaynah said: \"Those among our scholars who become corrupt are similar to the Jews, while those among our worshipers who become misguided are like Christians.\" Ibn Kathir: 2/335.\nWhat is the aim of warning against the conduct of rabbis and monks?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوٓاْ إِنَّ كَثِيرٗا مِّنَ ٱلۡأَحۡبَارِ وَٱلرُّهۡبَانِ لَيَأۡكُلُونَ أَمۡوَٰلَ ٱلنَّاسِ بِٱلۡبَٰطِلِ وَيَصُدُّونَ عَن سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِۗ وَٱلَّذِينَ يَكۡنِزُونَ ٱلذَّهَبَ وَٱلۡفِضَّةَ وَلَا يُنفِقُونَهَا فِي سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِ فَبَشِّرۡهُم بِعَذَابٍ أَلِيمٖ ٣٤\nPeople rely on their scholars, worshipers and the wealthy among them, and when these groups of people become corrupt, the society in general becomes corrupt. Ibn Kathir: 2/335.\nAllah warns against rabbis (scholars), monks (worshipers) and the wealthy. Why?\nوَٱلَّذِينَ يَكۡنِزُونَ ٱلذَّهَبَ وَٱلۡفِضَّةَ وَلَا يُنفِقُونَهَا فِي سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِ فَبَشِّرۡهُم بِعَذَابٍ أَلِيمٖ ٣٤ يَوۡمَ يُحۡمَىٰ عَلَيۡهَا فِي نَارِ جَهَنَّمَ فَتُكۡوَىٰ بِهَا جِبَاهُهُمۡ وَجُنُوبُهُمۡ وَظُهُورُهُمۡۖ هَٰذَا مَا كَنَزۡتُمۡ لِأَنفُسِكُمۡ فَذُوقُواْ مَا كُنتُمۡ تَكۡنِزُونَ ٣٥\nIt is said that he who covets something and prefers it to Allah's obedience, will be punished with it. Because hoarding money was better to these people than Allah's pleasure, they were punished with it. Money was precious to those who hoarded it in this life; therefore, it will become most harmful to them in the Hereafter. Ibn Kathir: 2/336.\nHe who covets a thing and prefers it to Allah's obedience, will be punished with it. Explain in the light of this verse.\nإِنَّ عِدَّةَ ٱلشُّهُورِ عِندَ ٱللَّهِ ٱثۡنَا عَشَرَ شَهۡرٗا فِي كِتَٰبِ ٱللَّهِ يَوۡمَ خَلَقَ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلۡأَرۡضَ مِنۡهَآ أَرۡبَعَةٌ حُرُمٞۚ\nThis verse indicates that it is obligatory to base the rulings in regard to acts of worship on the months and years known and used by the Arabs, (lunar-Hijri calendar), and not the calendars used by Persians, Romans or Copts. Al-Qurtubi: 10/197.\nThere are many calls to replace Arabic months with others, what is the Quranic guidance in this regard?\nوَقَٰتِلُواْ ٱلۡمُشۡرِكِينَ كَآفَّةٗ كَمَا يُقَٰتِلُونَكُمۡ كَآفَّةٗۚ وَٱعۡلَمُوٓاْ أَنَّ ٱللَّهَ مَعَ ٱلۡمُتَّقِينَ ٣٦\n(And know that Allah is with those who fear Him) with His help, support and aid. So let them strive to fear Allah in secret and in public, and obey Him. Especially when fighting the disbelievers, for in that situation, the believer may not be as conscious of Allah as he should when dealing with the enemy disbelievers who are waging war. Al-Saadi: 336.\nAfter the command to fight the disbelievers, they are commanded to fear Allah. Why?\nwords\nلِيُظهِرَهُTo make it prevail\nأَربَعَةٌ حُرُمٌFour sacred months during which Allah forbids fighting, they are: Thu al-Qa'dah,Thu al-Hajjah, Muharram, and Rajab."],[193,"§At-Tawbah\ndeeds\nGive a talk, or share a message about the risk of circumventing Sharia rulings, and the importance of being conscious of Allah.\nRecall the names of three countries or nations that were replaced by Allah when they replaced His Sharia with their whims, then invoke Allah by seeking refuge in His pleasure from His wrath, in His forgiveness from His punishment, from the loss of health, and from His sudden vengeance.\nLook for a sunnah of the Prophet (ﷺ) that you have not practiced yet, and do it.\nguid\nSociety has to reevaluate alien habits every now and then, as some of these habits may be false but have been normalized with time.\nBear in mind that it is Allah's way to replace sinners who have lost their way with better servants.\nGrief crushes one's spirit and weakens one's resolve and heart, thus it is incumbent upon the Muslim to dispel it, and help those around him do the same, as much as possible.\nrefl\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ مَا لَكُمۡ إِذَا قِيلَ لَكُمُ ٱنفِرُواْ فِي سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِ ٱثَّاقَلۡتُمۡ إِلَى ٱلۡأَرۡضِۚ أَرَضِيتُم بِٱلۡحَيَوٰةِ ٱلدُّنۡيَا مِنَ ٱلۡأٓخِرَةِۚ فَمَا مَتَٰعُ ٱلۡحَيَوٰةِ ٱلدُّنۡيَا فِي ٱلۡأٓخِرَةِ إِلَّا قَلِيلٌ ٣٨\nAllah admonishes them for preferring the comfort of this worldly life to the comfort in the Hereafter, whereas the comfort of the Hereafter can be attained only through the hardships of this worldly life. Al-Qurtubi: 10/208.\nHow can the comfort in the Hereafter be attained?\nإِلَّا تَنفِرُواْ يُعَذِّبۡكُمۡ عَذَابًا أَلِيمٗا\nFailing to go forth at a time when the command is announced a major sin that deserves the severest punishment because of the great harm to which it leads. The one who failed to go forth has disobeyed Allah, and did not help to support His religion or defend His Book and law. Moreover, He failed to help his Muslim brethren against their enemy who wants to eradicate them and destroy their religion. Furthermore, those who are weak in faith may follow his example and, what is worse, he may weaken the resolve of those who have gone forth to fight in Jihad against the enemies of Allah. Al-Saadi: 337.\nWhat is the risk of not responding to the call to go forth in the cause of Allah?\nإِلَّا تَنفِرُواْ يُعَذِّبۡكُمۡ عَذَابًا أَلِيمٗا وَيَسۡتَبۡدِلۡ قَوۡمًا غَيۡرَكُمۡ وَلَا تَضُرُّوهُ شَيۡـٔٗاۗ وَٱللَّهُ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ شَيۡءٖ قَدِيرٌ ٣٩\n(If you do not go forth, He will punish you with a painful punishment), that punishment can come directly from Him or at the hands of His servants. If people fail to go for Jihad in the cause of Allah, He may try them by causing enmity among themselves until it reaches persecution, as it is the reality of Muslims today. However, when they engage in Jihad, Allah will bring their hearts together, and make them strong against His and their enemy. Ibn Taimyah: 3/350.\nExplain the effect of failing to go for Jihad by listing the two types of possible punishments.\nإِلَّا تَنصُرُوهُ فَقَدۡ نَصَرَهُ ٱللَّهُ إِذۡ أَخۡرَجَهُ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ ثَانِيَ ٱثۡنَيۡنِ إِذۡ هُمَا فِي ٱلۡغَارِ إِذۡ يَقُولُ لِصَٰحِبِهِۦ لَا تَحۡزَنۡ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ مَعَنَاۖ\nAllah states that He is the guarantor of support to His Messenger (ﷺ) and His religion, whether people support His Messenger (ﷺ) or not. Since Allah has supported him when there were very few allies around him, and a great number of enemies chasing him, then He surely supports him today when he is with more allies and arms. Al-Baghawi: 2/282.\nSome Muslims think that Islam needs them; clarify the Quranic guidance in dealing with this thinking.\nإِذۡ هُمَا فِي ٱلۡغَارِ إِذۡ يَقُولُ لِصَٰحِبِهِۦ لَا تَحۡزَنۡ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ مَعَنَاۖ\n(Saying to his companion, \"Do not grieve\"), Abu Bakr As-Siddiq (t) was not only the Messenger's companion in the cave, but he was his absolute companion, who reached perfection in his companionship to the Prophet (ﷺ) in a manner with which no other person shared. Therefore, he was the perfect companion. Ibn Taimyah: 3/352.\nAbu Bakr As-Siddiq (t) was the perfect companion. Explain.\nلَا تَحۡزَنۡ\nThis verse states that grief may affect the sincerest of Allah's servants, even though it is more appropriate, if a person is faced with grief, to try to dispel it, because it causes one to lose courage and weakens one's resolve. Al-Saadi: 338.\nWhat is the risk of grieve to a Muslim? How should he deal with it?\nوَجَعَلَ كَلِمَةَ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ ٱلسُّفۡلَىٰۗ وَكَلِمَةُ ٱللَّهِ هِيَ ٱلۡعُلۡيَاۗ\nIt is the religion of Allah that will prevail, and be superior over all other religions, by means of clear proof and evidence, and by means of overwhelming force. Al-Saadi: 338.\nWhat are the means by which the religion of Islam will prevail?\nwords\nالنَّسِيءُPostponing of restriction within a sacred month to another\nلِيُوَاطِئُواSo they match\nعِدَّةَNumber of months\nاثَّاقَلتُمYou slacked off and became lazy\nإِلاَّ تَنفِرُواIf you do not go forth [to Jihad]"],[194,"§At-Tawbah\ndeeds\nDonate out of your money for charity, for it is Jihad with wealth.\nSeek refuge with Allah from incapacity and laziness, as they prevent one from worship.\nMake a plan, today, to prepare for doing good deeds, put your mind to it, and invoke Allah not to keep you away from achieving that due to your sins.\nguid\nJihad with wealth is a type of Jihad.\nGentle admonishment is permitted from one who loves and cares.\nOne's will to do good alone is not sufficient until it is backed by readiness to act.\nrefl\nٱنفِرُواْ خِفَافٗا وَثِقَالٗا وَجَٰهِدُواْ بِأَمۡوَٰلِكُمۡ وَأَنفُسِكُمۡ فِي سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِۚ ذَٰلِكُمۡ خَيۡرٞ لَّكُمۡ إِن كُنتُمۡ تَعۡلَمُونَ ٤١\nJihad with wealth precedes Jihad with lives, as Allah says, (and strive with your wealth and your lives in the cause of Allah), because one who strives with his wealth has, in fact, given out his wealth in the cause of Allah, and the one who strives with his life hopes to survive. Ibn Taimyah: 3/373.\nWhat is the importance of Jihad with wealth? Explain in the light of this verse.\nوَجَٰهِدُواْ بِأَمۡوَٰلِكُمۡ وَأَنفُسِكُمۡ فِي سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِۚ ذَٰلِكُمۡ خَيۡرٞ لَّكُمۡ إِن كُنتُمۡ تَعۡلَمُونَ ٤١\nThis is better for you in this life and in the Hereafter. You might spend small amounts, but Allah will reward you the property of your enemy in this life, as well as, the honor that He will keep for you in the Hereafter. Ibn Kathir: 2/344.\nGive an example of the virtues of Jihad in this life and in the Hereafter.\nعَفَا ٱللَّهُ عَنكَ لِمَ أَذِنتَ لَهُمۡ حَتَّىٰ يَتَبَيَّنَ لَكَ ٱلَّذِينَ صَدَقُواْ وَتَعۡلَمَ ٱلۡكَٰذِبِينَ ٤٣\nSufyan bin Uyaynah said: \"Reflect on the kindness of Allah; He starts with forgiveness before mentioning the sin.\" Al-Baghawi: 2/289.\nHow can we learn the etiquettes of admonishment from the style of the Quran?\nلَا يَسۡتَـٔۡذِنُكَ ٱلَّذِينَ يُؤۡمِنُونَ بِٱللَّهِ وَٱلۡيَوۡمِ ٱلۡأٓخِرِ أَن يُجَٰهِدُواْ بِأَمۡوَٰلِهِمۡ وَأَنفُسِهِمۡۗ\nAllah states that those who believe in Him and the Last Day do not ask for permission to stay behind from Jihad, and avoid offering their wealth and their lives, because of the desire that they have for good and their faith motivates them to strive in Jihad without anyone urging them, let alone asking to stay behind without an excuse. Al-Saadi: 338-339.\nTrue believers never ask to be excused from Jihad. Why?\nوَلَوۡ أَرَادُواْ ٱلۡخُرُوجَ لَأَعَدُّواْ لَهُۥ عُدَّةٗ وَلَٰكِن كَرِهَ ٱللَّهُ ٱنۢبِعَاثَهُمۡ فَثَبَّطَهُمۡ وَقِيلَ ٱقۡعُدُواْ مَعَ ٱلۡقَٰعِدِينَ ٤٦\nMeaning: If they intended Jihad, they would have prepared for the road, but neglecting the preparation was a proof that they intended to stay behind. Al-Qurtubi: 10/229.\nWhat is the sign of sincerity when intending to perform an act of worship?\nلَوۡ خَرَجُواْ فِيكُم مَّا زَادُوكُمۡ إِلَّا خَبَالٗا وَلَأَوۡضَعُواْ خِلَٰلَكُمۡ يَبۡغُونَكُمُ ٱلۡفِتۡنَةَ وَفِيكُمۡ سَمَّٰعُونَ لَهُمۡۗ وَٱللَّهُ عَلِيمُۢ بِٱلظَّٰلِمِينَ ٤٧\n(Had they gone forth), the hypocrites, (with you) to Jihad, (they would not have increased you except in confusion) causing chaos and corruption by exaggerating the matters to induce cowardice among the believers. (And they would have been active) they would have rushed, (among you) by gossiping to cause enmity and hatred among you. Al-Baghawi: 2/289.\nDescribe the effect of hypocrites in spreading gossip and corruption.\nوَفِيكُمۡ سَمَّٰعُونَ لَهُمۡۗ وَٱللَّهُ عَلِيمُۢ بِٱلظَّٰلِمِينَ ٤٧\nAllah states that there were among the believers some who responded and accepted what the hypocrites said. Since this had occurred at the times of the Prophet (ﷺ), then it is more likely to occur afterwards. Ibn Taimyah: 3/374.\nIs the risk of hypocrisy limited to the times of the Prophet (ﷺ). Explain.\nwords\nعَرَضًا قَرِيبًاAn easy gain of this worldly life\nالشُّقَّةُA hard distance\nانبِعَاثَهُمTheir going forth for Jihad\nفَثَبَّطَهُمHe made them lag behind\nخَبَالًاChaos and corruption\nوَلأَوضَعُوا خِلاَلَكُمThey would be active among you with gossip\nيَبغُونَكُمُ الفِتنَةَThey seek to cause fitnah among you"],[195,"§At-Tawbah\ndeeds\nGather the qualities of hypocrites in this Surah, and beware of committing them.\nReflect on this verse, and take its morals as a standard to follow.\nSupplicate Allah sincerely for martyrdom, and He will elevate you to the rank of martyrs.\nguid\nTwisting words, changing facts, and making up false narratives are all methods of hypocrites and their followers, be mindful of their ways lest you fall for their deception.\nA true believer rejoices in the prevalence of Allah's word and truth while a hypocrite does not.\nA sign of a believer's prayer is the fact that he performs it with dedication because of its great benefits to him.\nrefl\nلَقَدِ ٱبۡتَغَوُاْ ٱلۡفِتۡنَةَ مِن قَبۡلُ وَقَلَّبُواْ لَكَ ٱلۡأُمُورَ حَتَّىٰ جَآءَ ٱلۡحَقُّ وَظَهَرَ أَمۡرُ ٱللَّهِ وَهُمۡ كَٰرِهُونَ ٤٨\n(And devised plots against you), they thought hard, they were used to cause mischief in their attempts to undermine your call and harm your religion, and they did not spare any effort to do so. (Until the truth [victory] came and Allah’s decree prevailed, even though they were averse). Thus, their plot was foiled and their falsehood was diminished. Such people deserve that Allah should warn His believing servants against them. Al-Saadi: 339.\nHypocrites' plots are big, even though they end up in failure. Explain.\nأَلَا فِي ٱلۡفِتۡنَةِ سَقَطُواْۗ\nEven if we assume that the one who said this was sincere in his intention, staying behind would cause a greater evil and would definitely lead to greater mischief, namely disobedience toward Allah and His Messenger (ﷺ), and having the audacity to commit this great sin and tell this great lie. As for going forth, the negative consequences thereof are small in comparison to staying behind, and they are not real. Moreover, the aim of the one who said this was to stay behind, and nothing else. Al-Saadi: 339.\nHypocrites' views of sin are different from that of the believers. Explain.\nإِن تُصِبۡكَ حَسَنَةٞ تَسُؤۡهُمۡۖ وَإِن تُصِبۡكَ مُصِيبَةٞ يَقُولُواْ قَدۡ أَخَذۡنَآ أَمۡرَنَا مِن قَبۡلُ وَيَتَوَلَّواْ وَّهُمۡ فَرِحُونَ ٥٠\n(If good befalls you), a victory or booties of war, (it distresses them), it makes the hypocrites miserable. (But if disaster strikes you), a killing or defeat, (they say, \"We took our matter [in hand] before\"), we warned, (and turn away), they leave, (while they are rejoicing) happy for your disaster. Al-Baghawi: 2/290.\nSome people become happy for the disbelievers' victory and when disaster strikes some Muslims. Is that considered an attitude of believers?\nقُلۡ هَلۡ تَرَبَّصُونَ بِنَآ إِلَّآ إِحۡدَى ٱلۡحُسۡنَيَيۡنِۖ وَنَحۡنُ نَتَرَبَّصُ بِكُمۡ أَن يُصِيبَكُمُ ٱللَّهُ بِعَذَابٖ مِّنۡ عِندِهِۦٓ أَوۡ بِأَيۡدِينَاۖ فَتَرَبَّصُوٓاْ إِنَّا مَعَكُم مُّتَرَبِّصُونَ ٥٢\n(Say, \"Do you await for us except one of the two best things\"), do you await for us except two things: Victory and prevailing, or dying in the cause of Allah. Each one of these two things is actually great. (With punishment from Himself), which are disasters and what is sent down from Heavens, or the torment in the Hereafter. (Or at our hands), which is killing. (So wait), this is a threat. Ibn Juzay: 1/340.\nMuslim fighters wait for one of these two best things. What are they? The disbelievers wait for one of these two punishments. What are they?\nوَمَا مَنَعَهُمۡ أَن تُقۡبَلَ مِنۡهُمۡ نَفَقَٰتُهُمۡ إِلَّآ أَنَّهُمۡ كَفَرُواْ بِٱللَّهِ وَبِرَسُولِهِۦ\nThe disbeliever's deeds that are considered good such as maintaining kinship ties, mending the life of a broken person, and providing relief assistance to a stricken person, will not benefit him in the Hereafter, nor will he be rewarded for them; however, he is compensated for them in this worldly life. Al-Qurtubi: 8/161.\nHypocrites may do good deeds, but what prevents them from benefiting from them in the Hereafter?\nوَلَا يَأۡتُونَ ٱلصَّلَوٰةَ إِلَّا وَهُمۡ كُسَالَىٰ وَلَا يُنفِقُونَ إِلَّا وَهُمۡ كَٰرِهُونَ ٥٤\nThis is the utmost criticism of anyone who acts like they did. Moreover, it indicates that one should come to prayer with enthusiasm and energy, and spend willingly and readily, hoping to store up its reward with Allah alone, so that he does not resemble the hypocrites. Al-Saadi: 340.\nWhat should be the ideal approach to establishing prayer and spending for charity?\nوَلَا يُنفِقُونَ إِلَّا وَهُمۡ كَٰرِهُونَ ٥٤\nBecause they consider spending as a loss and abstaining from it as a gain. If this becomes one's intention, then his spending will not be accepted nor rewarded by Allah. Al-Qurtubi: 10/239.\nHypocrite's spending is not accepted. Why?\nwords\nوَقَلَّبُوا لَكَ الأُمُورَThey devised plots against you\nتَرَبَّصُونَYou await\nإِحدَى الحُسنَيَينِMartyrdom or victory"],[196,"§At-Tawbah\ndeeds\nReevaluate your way of handling things; do not overspend your money, nor spoil your children, and risk losing both. Do not overindulge them to the extent of bringing forth the wrath of Allah.\nShare a message in which you expose a trait of the heedless and hypocrites, that they look to those who are above them regarding worldly vanity only, and not to those who are above them in religion.\nConsider an old palace or a fancy classic car and think of its original owner; what was his fate? Will he be held accountable for owning it? What does he wish for, now?\nguid\nWorldly vanities are but a way to lure a disbelievers and the defiantly disobedient, so do not be deluded by them.\nAmong the traits of the heedless and the hypocrite is that if given something of worldly gains, he is pleased, and if not, he becomes enraged.\nAmong the traits of a hypocrite is criticizing the believers through subtle innuendo, and it takes a perceptive person to realize that.\nrefl\nفَلَا تُعۡجِبۡكَ أَمۡوَٰلُهُمۡ وَلَآ أَوۡلَٰدُهُمۡۚ إِنَّمَا يُرِيدُ ٱللَّهُ لِيُعَذِّبَهُم بِهَا فِي ٱلۡحَيَوٰةِ ٱلدُّنۡيَا وَتَزۡهَقَ أَنفُسُهُمۡ وَهُمۡ كَٰفِرُونَ ٥٥\nDo not be impressed by the wealth or children of these hypocrites, for there is no blessing in that. One of the serious evil consequences of them is that their hearts become attached to them, and their aspirations do not go beyond them, thus they become their ultimate goal, and there is no room left in their hearts for any thought of the Hereafter. This dictates that when they leave this world, their souls depart while they are still disbelievers. Al-Saadi: 340.\nHow do the wealth and children of hypocrites become a cause for their disbelief in Allah, the Almighty?\nفَلَا تُعۡجِبۡكَ أَمۡوَٰلُهُمۡ وَلَآ أَوۡلَٰدُهُمۡۚ إِنَّمَا يُرِيدُ ٱللَّهُ لِيُعَذِّبَهُم بِهَا فِي ٱلۡحَيَوٰةِ ٱلدُّنۡيَا وَتَزۡهَقَ أَنفُسُهُمۡ وَهُمۡ كَٰفِرُونَ ٥٥\nWhen Allah wants to gradually lead some people to destruction, He often increases their wealth and children. When they see their excess of wealth over the believers, they attribute that to being honored by Allah, so they continue down this path until they die. In fact, Allah does not want to reward them, rather, to try them. Al-Biqai: 3/334.\nIs the abundance of wealth and children a sign of Allah's pleasure with a servant?\nوَمِنۡهُم مَّن يَلۡمِزُكَ فِي ٱلصَّدَقَٰتِ فَإِنۡ أُعۡطُواْ مِنۡهَا رَضُواْ وَإِن لَّمۡ يُعۡطَوۡاْ مِنۡهَآ إِذَا هُمۡ يَسۡخَطُونَ ٥٨\nTheir pleasure and rage are for something other than Allah, and this is the case of one who is attached to authority, image, or similar things in accordance with his whims. If he gains it, then he is pleased, and if not, he becomes enraged. So, he is a slave of his whims because submissiveness is a deed of the heart, hence, whatever makes the heart submissive, then the heart, in turn, becomes a slave to it. Ibn Taimyah: 3/380.\nTrue submissiveness is a deed of the heart. Explain in light of the verse.\nفَإِنۡ أُعۡطُواْ مِنۡهَا رَضُواْ وَإِن لَّمۡ يُعۡطَوۡاْ مِنۡهَآ إِذَا هُمۡ يَسۡخَطُونَ ٥٨\nIt is inappropriate for a servant to be pleased or resentful on the basis of his own whims and desires, or for the sake of worldly matters and corrupt aims; rather, his inclinations should be in accordance with what pleases his Lord. Al-Saadi: 340.\nThe Muslim should always be rightfully content. How?\nوَمِنۡهُم مَّن يَلۡمِزُكَ فِي ٱلصَّدَقَٰتِ فَإِنۡ أُعۡطُواْ مِنۡهَا رَضُواْ وَإِن لَّمۡ يُعۡطَوۡاْ مِنۡهَآ إِذَا هُمۡ يَسۡخَطُونَ ٥٨\nMeaning: The hypocrite criticizes your distribution of charities and slanders you by saying that Muhammad gives only those whom he likes. Al-Baghawi: 2/293.\nCasting doubts on the intentions of today's scholars and preachers; is this a new or an old tactic?\nوَمِنۡهُمُ ٱلَّذِينَ يُؤۡذُونَ ٱلنَّبِيَّ وَيَقُولُونَ هُوَ أُذُنٞۚ قُلۡ أُذُنُ خَيۡرٖ لَّكُمۡ يُؤۡمِنُ بِٱللَّهِ وَيُؤۡمِنُ لِلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ\n(They say, \"He listens to everyone\"), he listens to everything said to him and believes it. (Say, \"He listens to what is best for you), he listens to the good and truth. (Trusts the believers), he believes what the believers say. Ibn Juzay: 1/262.\nWhy did the hypocrites describe the Prophet (ﷺ) as (he listens to everyone)? How did Allah respond to them?\nوَٱلَّذِينَ يُؤۡذُونَ رَسُولَ ٱللَّهِ لَهُمۡ عَذَابٌ أَلِيمٞ ٦١\nA painful punishment in this world and the Hereafter. Part of that painful punishment is that it is mandatory to execute the one who says offensive things about the Messenger (ﷺ), or impugns him. Al-Saadi: 342.\nGive an example of a painful punishment in this life for one who offends the Prophet (ﷺ).\nwords\nيَفرَقُونَThey are afraid\nمَلجَأًA refuge, a safe place\nمَغَارَاتٍCaves in mountains"],[197,"§At-Tawbah\ndeeds\nUsing a friendly approach, be keen today to enjoin good and forbid evil, in contrast to the hypocrites.\nGive to charity, in accordance to your means, make it a habit, and remember that hypocrites close their hands.\nRemember Allah often, today, to disavow hypocrisy, as a hypocrite is heedless of the remembrance of Allah, and rarely does that.\nguid\nA true believer is conscious of Allah, and a hypocrite is conscious of people. Each one strives to please whomever he is conscious of.\nMockery of Islamic rites and its followers may cause one to be thrown in the Fire, even if it is done jokingly.\nHypocrites have clear traits that distinguish them from true believers.\nrefl\nوَٱللَّهُ وَرَسُولُهُۥٓ أَحَقُّ أَن يُرۡضُوهُ إِن كَانُواْ مُؤۡمِنِينَ ٦٢\nBecause the believer does not give precedence to anything over pleasing his Lord and His Messenger (ﷺ); therefore, this indicates that they are not believers when they give precedence to pleasing anyone other than Allah and His Messenger (ﷺ). This is a defiance of Allah. Al-Saadi: 342.\nA sign of having a good discipline is to give precedence to pleasing Allah over anyone else. Explain.\nيَحۡذَرُ ٱلۡمُنَٰفِقُونَ أَن تُنَزَّلَ عَلَيۡهِمۡ سُورَةٞ تُنَبِّئُهُم بِمَا فِي قُلُوبِهِمۡۚ قُلِ ٱسۡتَهۡزِءُوٓاْ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ مُخۡرِجٞ مَّا تَحۡذَرُونَ ٦٤\nQatadah said: This Surah is called \"Al-Fadihah\" (the Exposer), because it exposed the hypocrites. Ibn Kathir: 2/351.\nWith every event, it is prudent to reflect on a certain Surah; when is it prudent to repeat the reflection on Surat At-Tawbah?\nيَحۡذَرُ ٱلۡمُنَٰفِقُونَ أَن تُنَزَّلَ عَلَيۡهِمۡ سُورَةٞ تُنَبِّئُهُم بِمَا فِي قُلُوبِهِمۡۚ قُلِ ٱسۡتَهۡزِءُوٓاْ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ مُخۡرِجٞ مَّا تَحۡذَرُونَ ٦٤\nThese verses indicate that whoever hide something in his heart, especially if that which is hidden is plotting against and ridiculing Allah's religion, His revelations and His Messenger (ﷺ), then Allah will expose it and make him known, and punish him severely. Al-Saadi: 343.\nMany moral scandals involving Christian priests and Shiat Imams surface more often. What is secret behind that?\nوَلَئِن سَأَلۡتَهُمۡ لَيَقُولُنَّ إِنَّمَا كُنَّا نَخُوضُ وَنَلۡعَبُۚ قُلۡ أَبِٱللَّهِ وَءَايَٰتِهِۦ وَرَسُولِهِۦ كُنتُمۡ تَسۡتَهۡزِءُونَ ٦٥ لَا تَعۡتَذِرُواْ قَدۡ كَفَرۡتُم بَعۡدَ إِيمَٰنِكُمۡۚ\nRidiculing Allah and His Messenger (ﷺ) constitutes disbelief that puts one beyond the pale of Islam, because the foundation of Islam is built on the veneration of Allah and respect for His religion and His Messenger (ﷺ), and any mockery thereof will be contrary to this principle and is in sharp contrast to it. Al-Saadi: 343.\nRidiculing Allah, His verses and His Messenger (ﷺ) constitutes disbelief that puts one beyond the pale of Islam, why?\nوَلَئِن سَأَلۡتَهُمۡ لَيَقُولُنَّ إِنَّمَا كُنَّا نَخُوضُ وَنَلۡعَبُۚ قُلۡ أَبِٱللَّهِ وَءَايَٰتِهِۦ وَرَسُولِهِۦ كُنتُمۡ تَسۡتَهۡزِءُونَ ٦٥ لَا تَعۡتَذِرُواْ قَدۡ كَفَرۡتُم بَعۡدَ إِيمَٰنِكُمۡۚ\nThis verse proves that whoever offends Allah's Messenger (ﷺ), whether seriously or jokingly, becomes certainly a disbeliever. Ibn Taimyah: 3/400.\nWhat is Sharia ruling on one who offends and disdains the Prophet (ﷺ)?\nقُلۡ أَبِٱللَّهِ وَءَايَٰتِهِۦ وَرَسُولِهِۦ كُنتُمۡ تَسۡتَهۡزِءُونَ ٦٥ لَا تَعۡتَذِرُواْ قَدۡ كَفَرۡتُم بَعۡدَ إِيمَٰنِكُمۡۚ\nIt is reported that Imam Al-Shafi'i was asked about someone who ridiculed some of Allah's verses; he replied: \"That is a disbeliever,\" and he quoted this verse as evidence of this ruling: (Say, \"Is it Allah and His verses and His Messenger that you were mocking?` Make no excuse; you disbelieved after your belief). Ibn Taimyah: 3/402.\nWhat is Sharia ruling on one who ridicules some of Allah's verses?\nنَسُواْ ٱللَّهَ فَنَسِيَهُمۡۚ\nThey neglected the obedience of Allah, so Allah left them out of His guidance and success in this life, out of His mercy in the Hereafter and ditched them in His punishment. Al-Baghawi: 2/302.\n\"A befitting recompense\"; explain in light of this verse.\nwords\nيُحَادِدِOpposes\nحَسبُهُمSufficient for them"],[198,"§At-Tawbah\ndeeds\nSeek a righteous company so that the allegiance to faith, which is ordained by Allah, is realized and make it permanent.\nShare messages in which you enjoin good, such as reminding people of an act of worship that they have been falling short in, or forbid evil, such as warning against a sin that has been normalized.\nSupplicate Allah to be pleased with you in this life and the Hereafter.\nguid\nTrue salvation in this life and the Hereafter is achieved only by following what the Messengers brought.\nRead the stories of the Prophets so that you will be among those who become admonished when the stories of Messengers and their nations are narrated.\nEnjoining what is right and forbidding what is evil is the most prominent trait that distinguishes between believers and hypocrites.\nrefl\nكَٱلَّذِينَ مِن قَبۡلِكُمۡ كَانُوٓاْ أَشَدَّ مِنكُمۡ قُوَّةٗ وَأَكۡثَرَ أَمۡوَٰلٗا وَأَوۡلَٰدٗا فَٱسۡتَمۡتَعُواْ بِخَلَٰقِهِمۡ فَٱسۡتَمۡتَعۡتُم بِخَلَٰقِكُمۡ كَمَا ٱسۡتَمۡتَعَ ٱلَّذِينَ مِن قَبۡلِكُم بِخَلَٰقِهِمۡ وَخُضۡتُمۡ كَٱلَّذِي خَاضُوٓاْۚ أُوْلَٰٓئِكَ حَبِطَتۡ أَعۡمَٰلُهُمۡ فِي ٱلدُّنۡيَا وَٱلۡأٓخِرَةِۖ وَأُوْلَٰٓئِكَ هُمُ ٱلۡخَٰسِرُونَ ٦٩\nWhat kept most Muslims from understanding the Quran is their belief that the narrations therein about past nations of all religions who were either rewarded or punished, are just for the purpose of storytelling. No, actually, that is not the aim; rather the aim is to take lessons and be alert to this nation's repetition of the same offences and wrongdoings that caused the demise of past nations. Al-Biqai: 3/347.\nWhat is the aim of narrations in the Quran about past nations?\nفَٱسۡتَمۡتَعۡتُم بِخَلَٰقِكُمۡ كَمَا ٱسۡتَمۡتَعَ ٱلَّذِينَ مِن قَبۡلِكُم بِخَلَٰقِهِمۡ\nAs for the believers, even though they may enjoy their share (of worldly pleasures) and whatever they are granted in this world, they do so in a way that helps them to obey Allah. With regard to the knowledge they have, it is the knowledge that they learned from the Messengers; this is the type of knowledge that helps them attain certain faith in all that they try to achieve, and helps them to argue on the basis of truth in order to refute falsehood. Al-Saadi: 343.\nThe believers and disbelievers enjoy the pleasures of life, but what is the difference?\nفَمَا كَانَ ٱللَّهُ لِيَظۡلِمَهُمۡ وَلَٰكِن كَانُوٓاْ أَنفُسَهُمۡ يَظۡلِمُونَ ٧٠\nThey wronged themselves by disbelief, denial, and ingratitude. They directed Allah's blessings toward ways for which they were not intended, hence they deserved the punishment. Al-Qasimi: 4/166.\nWhat are the indications of wronging oneself, and warranting punishment of disbelievers?\nوَٱلۡمُؤۡمِنُونَ وَٱلۡمُؤۡمِنَٰتُ بَعۡضُهُمۡ أَوۡلِيَآءُ بَعۡضٖۚ يَأۡمُرُونَ بِٱلۡمَعۡرُوفِ وَيَنۡهَوۡنَ عَنِ ٱلۡمُنكَرِ وَيُقِيمُونَ ٱلصَّلَوٰةَ وَيُؤۡتُونَ ٱلزَّكَوٰةَ وَيُطِيعُونَ ٱللَّهَ وَرَسُولَهُۥٓۚ\nAllah describes the bond between the believers as (allies of one another) indicating the allegiance to Islam, in which they are all equal, where none of them mimics the other, or follows him without guidance, and that manifests sincerity and support among themselves, in contrast to the hypocrites who mimic each other in their falsehood. Ibn Ashur: 10/262.\nThe verse describes the believers as (allies on one another). Why?\nوَٱلۡمُؤۡمِنُونَ وَٱلۡمُؤۡمِنَٰتُ بَعۡضُهُمۡ أَوۡلِيَآءُ بَعۡضٖۚ\nMeaning: Their hearts are united in mutual kindness, love and compassion. Al-Qurtubi: 10/298.\nWhat should be the true feeling of a believer's heart toward another believer?\nأُوْلَٰٓئِكَ سَيَرۡحَمُهُمُ ٱللَّهُۗ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ عَزِيزٌ حَكِيمٞ ٧١\nThis statement, (For Allah is All-Mighty, All-Wise) explains the preceding one, (they who will receive Allah's mercy). Allah benefits His allies because He is the All-Mighty, and places the right recompense because He is All-Wise. Ibn Ashur: 10/263.\nThis verse concluded with (Allah is All-Mighty, All-Wise); why?\nوَرِضۡوَٰنٞ مِّنَ ٱللَّهِ أَكۡبَرُۚ\nA pleasure from Allah is greater than all the delights that they are enjoying, for they cannot enjoy those delights except by seeing their Lord and by His being pleased with them, because this is the ultimate good that worshipers seek, and the end goal for which lovers strive. Hence, the good pleasure of the Lord of the earth and the heavens is greater than the delights of Paradise. Al-Saadi: 344.\nWhy is the pleasure from Allah described as greater than the Bliss of Gardens?\nwords\nفَاستَمتَعُوا بِخَلاَقِهِمThey enjoyed their share of this life’s joys\nوَخُضتُمYou have indulged in lies and idle talk\nحَبِطَتTheir deeds became worthless\nوَالمُؤتَفِكَاتِTowns of Prophet Lot, turned upside down"],[199,"§At-Tawbah\ndeeds\nContribute, today, to the strive against disbelievers and hypocrites, even with words in your gatherings, on websites or by phone messages.\nSummarize the traits of hypocrites mentioned on this page of the Quran.\nPerform an act of worship in secret, of which no one knows about except Allah.\nguid\nFrequent swearing is censured because it is perceived as lying, and the hypocrites do that often, but the believers reveres Allah and do not take swearing lightly.\nSickness and hypocrisy of the heart is a divine punishment for one who deviates from the straight path.\nDo not shy away from performing a small deed in the cause of Allah; what counts is the heart intention behind the deed, and not the quantity of deeds .\nrefl\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلنَّبِيُّ جَٰهِدِ ٱلۡكُفَّارَ وَٱلۡمُنَٰفِقِينَ وَٱغۡلُظۡ عَلَيۡهِمۡۚ وَمَأۡوَىٰهُمۡ جَهَنَّمُۖ وَبِئۡسَ ٱلۡمَصِيرُ ٧٣\nJihad against the disbelievers is by sword, and Jihad against the hypocrites is by speech unless they show what constitutes disbelief. Ibn Juzay: 1/364.\nHow should Jihad against the disbelievers and hypocrites be with?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلنَّبِيُّ جَٰهِدِ ٱلۡكُفَّارَ وَٱلۡمُنَٰفِقِينَ وَٱغۡلُظۡ عَلَيۡهِمۡۚ\nAllah commanded His Messenger (ﷺ) to strive hard against the disbelievers and the hypocrites and to be harsh against them. Allah also commanded him to be merciful with the believers who followed him. Ibn Kathir: 2/355.\nDealing of a Muslim with another is different from his dealing with a disbeliever and a hypocrite. How?\nيَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلنَّبِيُّ جَٰهِدِ ٱلۡكُفَّارَ وَٱلۡمُنَٰفِقِينَ وَٱغۡلُظۡ عَلَيۡهِمۡۚ\nThis Jihad includes physical Jihad and verbal one through debating. Whoever among them decides to take the Muslims on, may be fought physically and verbally, by the sword and by debate. Whoever chooses to yield to Islam, such as living under Muslim rule or by means of a covenant, may be striven against by means of debate and proof, explaining to him the beauty of Islam and the evil of ascribing partners to Allah and that of disbelief. Al-Saadi: 344.\nWhat are the stages of striving against disbelievers and hypocrites?\nيَحۡلِفُونَ بِٱللَّهِ مَا قَالُواْ وَلَقَدۡ قَالُواْ كَلِمَةَ ٱلۡكُفۡرِ وَكَفَرُواْ بَعۡدَ إِسۡلَٰمِهِمۡ\nAllah does not say \"after their belief\" because they used to say \"we believe\", but faith did not enter their hearts. Ibn Juzay: 1/364.\nAllah says, (after accepting Islam), and does not say, \"after their belief.\" Why?\nوَمِنۡهُم مَّنۡ عَٰهَدَ ٱللَّهَ لَئِنۡ ءَاتَىٰنَا مِن فَضۡلِهِۦ لَنَصَّدَّقَنَّ وَلَنَكُونَنَّ مِنَ ٱلصَّٰلِحِينَ ٧٥ فَلَمَّآ ءَاتَىٰهُم مِّن فَضۡلِهِۦ بَخِلُواْ بِهِۦ وَتَوَلَّواْ وَّهُم مُّعۡرِضُونَ ٧٦ فَأَعۡقَبَهُمۡ نِفَاقٗا فِي قُلُوبِهِمۡ إِلَىٰ يَوۡمِ يَلۡقَوۡنَهُۥ بِمَآ أَخۡلَفُواْ ٱللَّهَ مَا وَعَدُوهُ وَبِمَا كَانُواْ يَكۡذِبُونَ ٧٧\nTherefore, the believer should beware of this abhorrent attitude, whereby a person gives a promise to his Lord that if he gets some of what he wants, he will do such and such, but then he does not fulfill his promise, for perhaps Allah will punish him with hypocrisy as He punished these people. Al-Saadi: 345.\nDescribe the risk of breaking a promise with Allah and its punishment.\nفَأَعۡقَبَهُمۡ نِفَاقٗا فِي قُلُوبِهِمۡ إِلَىٰ يَوۡمِ يَلۡقَوۡنَهُۥ بِمَآ أَخۡلَفُواْ ٱللَّهَ مَا وَعَدُوهُ وَبِمَا كَانُواْ يَكۡذِبُونَ ٧٧\nThe verse expresses their lying as (their persistent lying) to indicate that lying exists solidly in them. The present tense form of the verb (lying) indicates repetition and recurrence. Ibn Ashur: 10/273.\nThe verse expresses their lying as (their persistent lying); why?\nٱلَّذِينَ يَلۡمِزُونَ ٱلۡمُطَّوِّعِينَ مِنَ ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ فِي ٱلصَّدَقَٰتِ وَٱلَّذِينَ لَا يَجِدُونَ إِلَّا جُهۡدَهُمۡ فَيَسۡخَرُونَ مِنۡهُمۡ سَخِرَ ٱللَّهُ مِنۡهُمۡ وَلَهُمۡ عَذَابٌ أَلِيمٌ ٧٩\nIf a person obeys Allah and does voluntary good deeds, then what we should do is to help and support him in his action, but these hypocrites intended to discourage them by criticizing and speaking negatively of them. Al-Saadi: 346.\nWhat is required of the believers when they see one who does a good deed? What is the lesson learned from this verse?\nwords\nنَقَمُواThey hated, resented\nفَأَعقَبَهُمHe penalized them\nيَلمِزُونَThose who disparage\nالمُطَّوِّعِينَThose who give big money for charity"],[200,"§At-Tawbah\ndeeds\nCompare the number of times you laughed with that when you wept out of fear of Allah during the last month.\nMaintain the obligatory prayers in congregation during hot and cold weather, and never miss them.\nPerform a good deed by which you strive against your self and comfort, such as fasting on a hot day, or going out to help out a needy or a distressed person, so that Allah would relieve your trouble.\nguid\nAmong the signs of sickness of the heart is the dislike to perform obedient acts and worships.\nAdmiring the state of life of the unbelievers is prohibited.\nConstantly, seeking to be relieved from performing an obligatory act of worship without a real and true excuse is a denounced behavior.\nrefl\nفَرِحَ ٱلۡمُخَلَّفُونَ بِمَقۡعَدِهِمۡ خِلَٰفَ رَسُولِ ٱللَّهِ وَكَرِهُوٓاْ أَن يُجَٰهِدُواْ بِأَمۡوَٰلِهِمۡ وَأَنفُسِهِمۡ فِي سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِ\nThis is worse than merely staying behind, because staying behind was prohibited, but what made it worse was being pleased with having done an act of disobedience, and rejoicing in it, (and disliked to strive with their wealth and their lives in the cause of Allah). This is in contrast to the believers who, if they stayed behind -even if that was with a valid excuse- would feel sad and be filled with sorrow for staying behind, and they would love to strive, offering their wealth and their lives in Allah's cause because of the faith in their hearts and of what they hoped for of the bounty, kindness and blessing of Allah. Al-Saadi: 346.\nWhat is the difference in the reaction of a believer and that of a hypocrite when they miss good deeds?\nفَرِحَ ٱلۡمُخَلَّفُونَ بِمَقۡعَدِهِمۡ خِلَٰفَ رَسُولِ ٱللَّهِ\nThis verse describes their situation as a rebuke to them that implies a threat. (Those who were left behind) indicates a disdain for them, and that they were left out of Allah's pleasure. The use of the term, (were left behind) is more suitable in this case than the term, \"stayed behind\". Rejoicing, in this case, was only done by a hypocrite, and therefore, the three Companions who remained behind and those with excuses were exonerated. Ibn Atiyah: 3/65.\nAllah says, (were left behind), not \"stayed behind\", why. What do we benefit from that?\nوَقَالُواْ لَا تَنفِرُواْ فِي ٱلۡحَرِّۗ قُلۡ نَارُ جَهَنَّمَ أَشَدُّ حَرّٗاۚ لَّوۡ كَانُواْ يَفۡقَهُونَ ٨١\nThus, they gave precedence to a brief and temporary comfort over a complete and eternal comfort. They were afraid of the heat from which one may protect himself by seeking shade, and which disappears in the early morning and late afternoon, yet they did not fear the intense heat, the severity of which cannot be estimated, namely the fire of Hell. Al-Saadi: 346.\nWhat is reason for describing the hypocrites as unable to understand?\nفَلۡيَضۡحَكُواْ قَلِيلٗا وَلۡيَبۡكُواْ كَثِيرٗا جَزَآءَۢ بِمَا كَانُواْ يَكۡسِبُونَ ٨٢\nThe Companions were used to laugh, but frequent and habitual laughter is censured. It is normally associated with fools and idlers. It is said that frequent laughter causes the heart to be dead (indifferent). Al-Qurtubi: 10/318.\nExplain how should the believer manage laughter.\nإِنَّكُمۡ رَضِيتُم بِٱلۡقُعُودِ أَوَّلَ مَرَّةٖ فَٱقۡعُدُواْ مَعَ ٱلۡخَٰلِفِينَ ٨٣\nAny one who is reluctant and decline to participate in doing good deed that has been enjoined when the opportunity arises to do it, will not be helped after that, and will be deprived of doing it on subsequent occasions. Al-Saadi: 346.\nWhat is the risk of declining to participate in doing good deed when the right opportunity comes?\nوَلَا تُصَلِّ عَلَىٰٓ أَحَدٖ مِّنۡهُم مَّاتَ أَبَدٗا وَلَا تَقُمۡ عَلَىٰ قَبۡرِهِۦٓۖ إِنَّهُمۡ كَفَرُواْ بِٱللَّهِ وَرَسُولِهِۦ وَمَاتُواْ وَهُمۡ فَٰسِقُونَ ٨٤\nThe proper act of Sunnah when visiting Muslims' graves is invoking Allah to have mercy upon them, which is similar to performing funeral prayer before the burial. Allah says, (Never offer the funeral prayer for any of them who dies, nor stand by his grave). So, it is inferred from this that invoking Allah to have mercy upon the dead believers is ordained. Ibn Taimyah: 3/435.\nWhat is Sharia ruling on praying for the believers at their gravesites?\nوَلَا تُعۡجِبۡكَ أَمۡوَٰلُهُمۡ وَأَوۡلَٰدُهُمۡۚ إِنَّمَا يُرِيدُ ٱللَّهُ أَن يُعَذِّبَهُم بِهَا فِي ٱلدُّنۡيَا وَتَزۡهَقَ أَنفُسُهُمۡ وَهُمۡ كَٰفِرُونَ ٨٥\nThis is a lesson for believers that liking and disliking should be for the sake of Allah, as it is one of the most subtle and important concepts in Islamic faith. It is a concept upon which most subject matters in Islam are built, and from which most benefits and etiquettes are attained. That is because when one sees another who has been given worldly gains and thinks that he is among those who will be saved, then, he becomes affectionate toward him for his good speech while being heedless of his bad actions. Al-Biqai: 3/371.\nHow do we infer from this verse the belief of allegiance and renunciation?\nwords\nبِمَقعَدِهِمTheir staying behind\nخِلاَفَIn opposite of\nالخَالِفِينَThose who stay behind\nأُولُو الطَّولِThose who are wealthy"],[201,"§At-Tawbah\ndeeds\nSay, \"O Changer of the hearts, make my heart firm upon Your religion; O Allah, set right my heart for me.\"\nRead a book, or listen to an audio clip that boosts your drive for doing good deeds, such as books of Sunnah and biographies of scholars. Settling for less and committing a sinful act is a trait of hypocrites, not of the believers.\nPerform a good deed that helps to set right your heart, such as visiting a grave yard, and helping a needy person, or similar deeds.\nguid\nWhatever wealth you have is a trial for you, so spend it on things that please Allah and His Messenger (ﷺ), even if you may dislike these things.\nThe Companions wept for missing out on a good deed, despite the fact that they were excused. Have you ever wept for missing out on a good deed?\nDo not make false or deceiving excuses, for Allah knows the secret and what is even more hidden.\nrefl\nرَضُواْ بِأَن يَكُونُواْ مَعَ ٱلۡخَوَالِفِ\nMeaning: If war starts, such people are the most coward, but during peaceful times, they are the most boastful among people. Ibn Kathir: 2/363.\nWhat is the difference between a believer and a hypocrite at the times of war and peace?\nلَّيۡسَ عَلَى ٱلضُّعَفَآءِ وَلَا عَلَى ٱلۡمَرۡضَىٰ وَلَا عَلَى ٱلَّذِينَ لَا يَجِدُونَ مَا يُنفِقُونَ حَرَجٌ إِذَا نَصَحُواْ لِلَّهِ وَرَسُولِهِۦۚ\n(As long as they are sincere to Allah and His Messenger), they are sincere in their intention and love for Allah and His Messenger (ﷺ). Ibn Taimyah: 3/437.\nWhat is meant by: (as long as they are sincere to Allah and His Messenger)?\nلَّيۡسَ عَلَى ٱلضُّعَفَآءِ وَلَا عَلَى ٱلۡمَرۡضَىٰ وَلَا عَلَى ٱلَّذِينَ لَا يَجِدُونَ مَا يُنفِقُونَ حَرَجٌ إِذَا نَصَحُواْ لِلَّهِ وَرَسُولِهِۦۚ مَا عَلَى ٱلۡمُحۡسِنِينَ مِن سَبِيلٖۚ وَٱللَّهُ غَفُورٞ رَّحِيمٞ ٩١\n(As long as they are sincere to Allah), they are sincere in their words and actions, even if they could not go forth in Jihad. (There is no blame on those who do good), Allah described them as those who do good because they were sincere to Him and His Messenger (ﷺ). He spared them punishment, censure and blame. Ibn Juzay: 1/367.\nWhat is reason for describing the weak, the sick, and poor as (those who do good), despite the fact that they did not fight nor spent anything?\nمَا عَلَى ٱلۡمُحۡسِنِينَ مِن سَبِيلٖۚ وَٱللَّهُ غَفُورٞ رَّحِيمٞ ٩١\n(And Allah is All-Forgiving, Most Merciful) indicates that Man has inherent weakness and shortcomings despite his efforts, and hence Allah's forgiveness is most suitable for him. Al-Biqai: 3/374.\nWhat is wisdom behind concluding this verse with: (All-Forgiving), and (Most Merciful)?\nوَلَا عَلَى ٱلَّذِينَ إِذَا مَآ أَتَوۡكَ لِتَحۡمِلَهُمۡ قُلۡتَ لَآ أَجِدُ مَآ أَحۡمِلُكُمۡ عَلَيۡهِ تَوَلَّواْ وَّأَعۡيُنُهُمۡ تَفِيضُ مِنَ ٱلدَّمۡعِ حَزَنًا أَلَّا يَجِدُواْ مَا يُنفِقُونَ ٩٢\nThere is no blame on these people, and since there is no blame on them, the matter reverts to the original principle, which is that whoever intends good, accompanied by a firm resolve in the sense that he tries to do whatever he can, but is not able to achieve that, is regarded as being like the one who did it completely and achieved results. Al-Saadi: 348.\nIn light of this verse, what is importance of sincere intention?\nوَلَا عَلَى ٱلَّذِينَ إِذَا مَآ أَتَوۡكَ لِتَحۡمِلَهُمۡ قُلۡتَ لَآ أَجِدُ مَآ أَحۡمِلُكُمۡ عَلَيۡهِ تَوَلَّواْ وَّأَعۡيُنُهُمۡ تَفِيضُ مِنَ ٱلدَّمۡعِ حَزَنًا أَلَّا يَجِدُواْ مَا يُنفِقُونَ ٩٢\nThey were seven individuals called \"the weepers.\" They came to Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) and said: \"Allah enjoined us to go forth with you, so give us a ride.\" The Prophet (ﷺ) replied, as the verse states, (I can find no mounts for you), so they went back weeping. Al-Baghawi: 2/315.\nWe have seen, presently, some who weep over a lost match by their sports team, a lost desire or a missed worldly gain. What did the Companions (j) weep for?\nإِنَّمَا ٱلسَّبِيلُ عَلَى ٱلَّذِينَ يَسۡتَـٔۡذِنُونَكَ وَهُمۡ أَغۡنِيَآءُۚ رَضُواْ بِأَن يَكُونُواْ مَعَ ٱلۡخَوَالِفِ وَطَبَعَ ٱللَّهُ عَلَىٰ قُلُوبِهِمۡ فَهُمۡ لَا يَعۡلَمُونَ ٩٣\n(They do not know), they do not have the right knowledge, and that is why they were ignorant of the benefits of Jihad in this life and the Hereafter; therefore, they were content with which no wise person would be. This is more forceful description than what was stated earlier, (they do not understand). Al-Biqai: 3/375.\nWhat is wisdom behind concluding this verse with describing them as : (They do not know), and earlier as: (they do not understand)?\nwords\nالمُعَذِّرُونَThose who made excuses\nنَصَحُوا لِلَّهِThey are sincere to Allah"],[202,"§At-Tawbah\ndeeds\nDo a good deed in private, today, that no one knows about except Allah.\nToday, say often in your prayer, \"O my Lord, increase my knowledge.\"\nGive to charity, today, while realizing that your charity brings you nearer to Allah.\nguid\nBeing conscious of Allah is a reason for doing things right.\nSeeking to please Allah takes precedence over pleasing people. When Allah is pleased with someone, He makes pious people pleased with him too.\nBeing closer to scholars and to those who call others to Allah is a reason for gaining knowledge.\nrefl\nوَسَيَرَى ٱللَّهُ عَمَلَكُمۡ وَرَسُولُهُۥ\nDeeds are the criterion that distinguishes between sincerity and insincerity. As for mere words, they do not indicate anything. Al-Saadi: 348.\nWhat is the criterion for distinguishing between sincerity and insincerity toward religion?\nيَحۡلِفُونَ لَكُمۡ لِتَرۡضَوۡاْ عَنۡهُمۡۖ فَإِن تَرۡضَوۡاْ عَنۡهُمۡ فَإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ لَا يَرۡضَىٰ عَنِ ٱلۡقَوۡمِ ٱلۡفَٰسِقِينَ ٩٦\nOur satisfaction with a defiantly disobedient people is not something that pleases Allah when He is not satisfied with them. Ibn Taimyah: 3/438.\nIs it permitted to be satisfied with a defiantly disobedient people? Does that benefit them?\nٱلۡأَعۡرَابُ أَشَدُّ كُفۡرٗا وَنِفَاقٗا وَأَجۡدَرُ أَلَّا يَعۡلَمُواْ حُدُودَ مَآ أَنزَلَ ٱللَّهُ عَلَىٰ رَسُولِهِۦۗ\nThat is because they are far from listening to the Quran and learning Sunnah. Al-Baghawi: 2/317.\nFor someone who is far from circles of knowledge and scholars, how does that affect him?\nٱلۡأَعۡرَابُ أَشَدُّ كُفۡرٗا وَنِفَاقٗا وَأَجۡدَرُ أَلَّا يَعۡلَمُواْ حُدُودَ مَآ أَنزَلَ ٱللَّهُ عَلَىٰ رَسُولِهِۦۗ\nThis verse is proof of the virtue of knowledge; the one who lacks knowledge is closer to evil than the one who has knowledge, because Allah criticizes the Bedouins and stated that they are more stubborn in disbelief and hypocrisy, and He says that the reason for that is that they are more likely to be unaware of the limits prescribed by Allah in what He has revealed to His Messenger (ﷺ). Al-Saadi: 349.\nThis verse proves the virtue of knowledge. How?\nوَمِنَ ٱلۡأَعۡرَابِ مَن يَتَّخِذُ مَا يُنفِقُ مَغۡرَمٗا وَيَتَرَبَّصُ بِكُمُ الدَّوآئٍر عَلَيِهم دائِرة السَّوءِ واللَّهُ سَمِيعٌ عَلِيمٌ\n(And among the Bedouins are some who consider what they spend as a loss), which means giving zakah and spending in the cause of Allah become as heavy as taking a loss. (And await some misfortune to befall you), waits for a disaster to strike you. (May ill-fortune befall them), this is a notification from Allah. Ibn Juzay: 1/368.\nWhat do you think of one who claims to be a Muslim while he is glad to see disasters strike Muslims?\nوَمِنَ ٱلۡأَعۡرَابِ مَن يَتَّخِذُ مَا يُنفِقُ مَغۡرَمٗا\nThe believer should do the duties that are required of him willingly and with peace of mind, and should regard that as an opportunity, not as a penalty. Al-Saadi: 349.\nWhat should be the Muslim demeanor when performing required duties?\nوَمِنَ ٱلۡأَعۡرَابِ مَن يُؤۡمِنُ بِٱللَّهِ وَٱلۡيَوۡمِ ٱلۡأٓخِرِ وَيَتَّخِذُ مَا يُنفِقُ قُرُبَٰتٍ عِندَ ٱللَّهِ وَصَلَوَٰتِ ٱلرَّسُولِۚ\n(And of [obtaining] invocations of the Messenger), a reason for obtaining the invocations of the Prophet (ﷺ) because he used to supplicate Allah to bless and forgive those who spent in the cause of Allah. Therefore, it is recommended for one who receives charity to pray for the giver. Al-Alusi: 11/11.\nWhat is recommended for one who receives charity to say to the giver?\nwords\nلَن نُؤمِنَ لَكُمWe will not believe you\nوَأَجدَرُAnd more likely\nمَغرَمًاA loss\nوَيَتَرَبَّصُHe awaits\nالدَّوَائِرَMisfortune\nعَلَيهِم دَائِرَةُ السَّوءِMay ill-fortune befall them"],[203,"§At-Tawbah\ndeeds\nBe a forerunner, today, in doing a good deed, or participating in a project for preaching to Islam so that you be considered with the forerunners.\nShare a message in which you eulogize the Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ), proclaim their great deeds, and respond to those who abuse them.\nGive to charity in the hope of cleansing and purifying your heart, so that Allah may grant you your hope.\nguid\nFollowing the example of the Companions and their followers is the approach of Ahl Al-Sunnah, and it is the way to attain the pleasure of Allah.\nAllah is pleased with the Companions, so whoever is pleased with them will be close to Allah, and whoever is discontent with them will be far from Allah.\nThe motivator for one's apparent actions is what he conceals.\nrefl\nوَٱلسَّٰبِقُونَ ٱلۡأَوَّلُونَ مِنَ ٱلۡمُهَٰجِرِينَ وَٱلۡأَنصَارِ وَٱلَّذِينَ ٱتَّبَعُوهُم بِإِحۡسَٰنٖ رَّضِيَ ٱللَّهُ عَنۡهُمۡ وَرَضُواْ عَنۡهُ وَأَعَدَّ لَهُمۡ جَنَّٰتٖ تَجۡرِي تَحۡتَهَا ٱلۡأَنۡهَٰرُ خَٰلِدِينَ فِيهَآ أَبَدٗاۚ ذَٰلِكَ ٱلۡفَوۡزُ ٱلۡعَظِيمُ ١٠٠\nIt is a great righteous deed to be among the forerunners in emigration which in itself a hard thing to do, and goes against one's nature. So, whoever has done it first, sets an example for others to follow him in this good deed. Al-Qasimi: 4/191.\nAllah assigns a great reward and bounty for a forerunner in emigration and help in His cause. Why?\nوَٱلسَّٰبِقُونَ ٱلۡأَوَّلُونَ مِنَ ٱلۡمُهَٰجِرِينَ وَٱلۡأَنصَارِ وَٱلَّذِينَ ٱتَّبَعُوهُم بِإِحۡسَٰنٖ رَّضِيَ ٱللَّهُ عَنۡهُمۡ وَرَضُواْ عَنۡهُ\nAllah is pleased with the forerunners unconditionally while He would be pleased with those who follow them in the condition that they follow and do good. Allah's pleasure is an eternal Attribute of Him, which applies only to a servant whom Allah knows that he fulfills the requirements of His pleasure. When Allah is pleased with a servant, He will never be angry with him. Ibn Taimyah: 3/440.\nIn light of this verse, explain the virtue of the Prophet's Companions?\nوَمِمَّنۡ حَوۡلَكُم مِّنَ ٱلۡأَعۡرَابِ مُنَٰفِقُونَۖ وَمِنۡ أَهۡلِ ٱلۡمَدِينَةِ مَرَدُواْ عَلَى ٱلنِّفَاقِ لَا تَعۡلَمُهُمۡۖ نَحۡنُ نَعۡلَمُهُمۡۚ سَنُعَذِّبُهُم مَّرَّتَيۡنِ ثُمَّ يُرَدُّونَ إِلَىٰ عَذَابٍ عَظِيمٖ ١٠١\nThey are punished twice because they combined disbelief with hypocrisy. Al-Qasimi: 4/193.\nWhat is the reason for doubling the punishment in this verse, (We will punish them twice, then they will be brought back to a great punishment)?\nوَءَاخَرُونَ ٱعۡتَرَفُواْ بِذُنُوبِهِمۡ خَلَطُواْ عَمَلٗا صَٰلِحٗا وَءَاخَرَ سَيِّئًا عَسَى ٱللَّهُ أَن يَتُوبَ عَلَيۡهِمۡۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ غَفُورٞ رَّحِيمٌ ١٠٢\nThis verse indicates that the one who mixes righteous deeds with evil ones but recognizes that, and is remorseful but does not repent sincerely, is subject to both fear (of punishment) and hope (of protection therefrom), but he is closer to salvation. As for the one who mixes his deeds but does not acknowledge them or feel any remorse for what he has done in the past, and persists in sin, there is a great fear that punishment will reach him. Al-Saadi: 350.\nWhat are the two types of those who mix righteous deeds with evil ones?\nخُذۡ مِنۡ أَمۡوَٰلِهِمۡ صَدَقَةٗ تُطَهِّرُهُمۡ وَتُزَكِّيهِم بِهَا وَصَلِّ عَلَيۡهِمۡۖ\n(Take charity from their wealth to cleanse [them]), cleanse them from their sins. (And purify them) to elevate them from the levels of hypocrites to the ranks of the sincere ones. Al-Baghawi: 2/322.\nState some of the blessings that reach the believer when he spends for charity ?\nخُذۡ مِنۡ أَمۡوَٰلِهِمۡ صَدَقَةٗ تُطَهِّرُهُمۡ وَتُزَكِّيهِم بِهَا وَصَلِّ عَلَيۡهِمۡۖ إِنَّ صَلَوٰتَكَ سَكَنٞ لَّهُمۡۗ\nIt is encouraged for the ruler or his deputy to offer supplication for blessing upon the one who gives his zakah, and that it should be done out loud so that the giver can hear it and be comforted by it. From this, it is learned that it is good to try to make the believer happy by saying gentle words, praying for him, and other things that bring reassurance and comfort to his heart. It is also good to encourage those who give of their wealth and do righteous deeds by offering supplication for them, praising them, and similar acts. Al-Saadi: 351.\nWhat is the benefit of supplication of the receiver of zakah for the giver?\nوَقُلِ ٱعۡمَلُواْ فَسَيَرَى ٱللَّهُ عَمَلَكُمۡ وَرَسُولُهُۥ وَٱلۡمُؤۡمِنُونَۖ وَسَتُرَدُّونَ إِلَىٰ عَٰلِمِ ٱلۡغَيۡبِ وَٱلشَّهَٰدَةِ فَيُنَبِّئُكُم بِمَا كُنتُمۡ تَعۡمَلُونَ ١٠٥\nAfter their repentance is accepted, they were commanded to prove their sincerity by actions, and show their utmost desire to elevate themselves to the ranks of perfection, so that they draw level with those who preceded them; which is the intended aim. Ibn Ashur: 11/25.\nAfter their repentance is accepted, the believers were commanded to do as they will. Why?\nwords\nمَرَدُواThey are obstinate [in their hypocrisy]\nوَتُزَكِّيهِم بِهَاYou elevate them from levels of hypocrites\nوَصَلِّ عَلَيهِمPray for them\nسَكَنٌ لَهُمA source of mercy and comfort for them\nمُرجَونَThey are deferred"],[204,"§At-Tawbah\ndeeds\nWrite a documented letter in which you expose one of the hypocrites' projects.\nLend a helping hand, today, to an organization of which its operators are known for their goodness and righteousness.\nTry to maintain your purity all day today, if you can without hardship.\nguid\nAnyone who reflects on the meanings of the Holy Quran is not easily deceived by the hypocrites' flashy slogans and their pretenses of doing good.\nDo not be of any help to those who want to break up the Muslim society, corrupt its generation, exploit its women, and remember what Allah said to His Prophet (ﷺ):\nInvoke Allah to make your deeds based on fearing Him, seeking His pleasure and being sincere to Him.\nrefl\nوَٱلَّذِينَ ٱتَّخَذُواْ مَسۡجِدٗا ضِرَارٗا وَكُفۡرٗا وَتَفۡرِيقَۢا بَيۡنَ ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ وَإِرۡصَادٗا لِّمَنۡ حَارَبَ ٱللَّهَ وَرَسُولَهُۥ مِن قَبۡلُۚ وَلَيَحۡلِفُنَّ إِنۡ أَرَدۡنَآ إِلَّا ٱلۡحُسۡنَىٰۖ وَٱللَّهُ يَشۡهَدُ إِنَّهُمۡ لَكَٰذِبُونَ ١٠٧\nThis, also, applies to whoever erected buildings emulating Muslims Mosques but for different purposes, such as shrines and similar things, etc. Especially, if they cause harm, disbelief and create division among the believers, and as a base for hypocrites and innovators, which makes these building very similar to the Masjid al-Dhirar (harm). Ibn Taimyah: 3/447.\nCan the buildings that spread the falsehood of innovators be considered mosques of harm? Why?\nوَٱلَّذِينَ ٱتَّخَذُواْ مَسۡجِدٗا ضِرَارٗا وَكُفۡرٗا وَتَفۡرِيقَۢا بَيۡنَ ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ\nThat is to separate the Muslim congregation for prayer so that some groups of them would stay away from the Prophet (ﷺ). This proves that the primary goal and main objective of the congregation for prayer is bringing the hearts and minds together in obedience. Al-Baghawi: 2/366.\nWhat is the main objective of ordaining prayer in congregation? How does Sharia maintain this objective?\nلَا تَقُمۡ فِيهِ أَبَدٗاۚ لَّمَسۡجِدٌ أُسِّسَ عَلَى ٱلتَّقۡوَىٰ مِنۡ أَوَّلِ يَوۡمٍ أَحَقُّ أَن تَقُومَ فِيهِۚ\nSin has an impact on places, as the sin of the hypocrites had an impact on that mosque that was built for the purpose of mischief. Thus, it was prohibited to pray therein. Similarly, obedience has an impact on places, as was the case with regard to the mosque of Quba', of which Allah said, (A mosque that was founded on piety from the first day is more deserving of you to pray therein). Hence Masjid Quba' enjoys a special standing that is not shared with any other mosque, as the Prophet (ﷺ) used to visit Quba' every Saturday to pray there, and he encouraged Muslims to do the same. Al-Saadi: 352.\nPlaces are impacted by the blessing of obedience and the evil of sin. Explain.\nلَّمَسۡجِدٌ أُسِّسَ عَلَى ٱلتَّقۡوَىٰ مِنۡ أَوَّلِ يَوۡمٍ أَحَقُّ أَن تَقُومَ فِيهِۚ\nThis verse validates the decision of the Companions (j) along with Omar (t) when he consulted with them about the starting date of the Muslim calendar, and they all agreed on the year of Hijrah (Prophet's migration from Makkah to Al-Madinah) because that was the time when Allah strengthen Islam. Their decision coincided with the meaning of this verse. Now we know that (from the first day) means the first day of our Hijri calendar. Al-Alusi: 11/31.\nState an example showing the subtle understanding of the Quran by the Companions (j), and their adherence to it.\nفِيهِ رِجَالٞ يُحِبُّونَ أَن يَتَطَهَّرُواْۚ وَٱللَّهُ يُحِبُّ ٱلۡمُطَّهِّرِينَ ١٠٨\nIn this verse, Allah commends those who loved purity, and preferred cleansing, as this is considered a human nobility and an ordained act of Sharia. Al-Qurtubi: 10/381.\nAccording to Islam, what is the importance of purity?\nأَفَمَنۡ أَسَّسَ بُنۡيَٰنَهُۥ عَلَىٰ تَقۡوَىٰ مِنَ ٱللَّهِ وَرِضۡوَٰنٍ خَيۡرٌ أَم مَّنۡ أَسَّسَ بُنۡيَٰنَهُۥ عَلَىٰ شَفَا جُرُفٍ هَارٖ فَٱنۡهَارَ بِهِۦ فِي نَارِ جَهَنَّمَۗ وَٱللَّهُ لَا يَهۡدِي ٱلۡقَوۡمَ ٱلظَّٰلِمِينَ ١٠٩\nLaying the foundation of a building on piety and seeking Allah's pleasure is achieved through sincere intention for the sake of Allah, and spreading His words. Laying the foundation of a building on the edge of a crumbling precipice is done through corrupt intention, pretension, and creating division among the believers. That is all metaphorically speaking. Ibn Juzay: 1/369.\nWhen is a building founded on piety? When is it founded on a crumbling precipice?\nإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ ٱشۡتَرَىٰ مِنَ ٱلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ أَنفُسَهُمۡ وَأَمۡوَٰلَهُم بِأَنَّ لَهُمُ ٱلۡجَنَّةَۚ يُقَٰتِلُونَ فِي سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِ فَيَقۡتُلُونَ وَيُقۡتَلُونَۖ وَعۡدًا عَلَيۡهِ حَقّٗا فِي ٱلتَّوۡرَىٰةِ وَٱلۡإِنجِيلِ وَٱلۡقُرۡءَانِۚ وَمَنۡ أَوۡفَىٰ بِعَهۡدِهِۦ مِنَ ٱللَّهِۚ فَٱسۡتَبۡشِرُواْ بِبَيۡعِكُمُ ٱلَّذِي بَايَعۡتُم بِهِۦۚ وَذَٰلِكَ هُوَ ٱلۡفَوۡزُ ٱلۡعَظِيمُ ١١١\nIf you want to know how great this deal is, then look at who the purchaser is: Allah, the Almighty. Look at the price, for it is the greatest of prices: Gardens of eternal bliss. Look at what you pay for it, namely your lives and your wealth, which are the dearest of all things to men. Look at the one at whose hands this transaction was done, for he is the noblest of the Messengers. Look at the Books in which it was written down, for they are the great Books of Allah that were sent down to the best of creation. Al-Saadi: 353.\nHow big is this great deal between Allah and the believers?\nwords\nضِرَارًاTo cause harm [to the believers]\nوَإِرصَادًاIn anticipation\nشَفَاAn edge\nجُرُفٍ هَارA crumbling precipice"]])